window.BRECHAS_DETAIL_EN={"MX-001":{"tit":"Client report generation","actual":"Drives per client, category, or as requested by the client or authority. Currently, clients or authorities request various information according to their needs (season, internal matters, pending merchandise, high-impact crimes, etc.), which we handle through drives that we try to keep updated daily, or that we build from scratch in some cases.","futura":"Being able to download any report, in any category, in real time from Discovery.","gap":"Improve efficiency for the back-office team in administrative work. Reduce manual creation that relies on outdated information.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"Important for strengthening operational efficiency and information analysis, especially during peak seasons and key dates, enabling access to real-time data and avoiding reliance on manual files for report generation. Additionally, this information can generate value for the Marketing area, facilitating preventive analyses and the production of client communications more agilely.","CL":"Although this process is currently handled through dashboards that automatically process the data required for report generation, there is convergence. We work this way; perhaps we just need to refine it a bit more so it is truly real-time, as we generally have all the elements in place for that to happen. Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — This functionality partially exists in Alliance and was implemented by Ale's BI team. Follow the path \"Discovery\" > \"My Associated Reports\". Not relevant to USA operations, as data must be verified before being sent to clients."}},"MX-002":{"tit":"Appointment scheduling and assignment","actual":"Appointments are currently scheduled by email sent to various recipients, primarily Legal Guard (Guardia Legal), their coordinator, and/or the coordination teams — in some cases using a specific format sent to asesoriascae@altomexico.com.mx. Legal Guard manually reviews these emails, enters the information into a Drive or Excel file, and compiles the appointment schedule, which is sent out daily between 06:00 and 06:30 to the coordination teams so they can filter by day and area and assign appointments to their teams. In this workflow, data entry is often performed while handling multiple simultaneous tasks, which leads to errors, delays, and the risk of misentry or missed entries when an email falls out of sight. Additionally, appointments are sometimes scheduled in incorrect states due to unfamiliarity with locations, meaning there is no 100% certainty of full appointment coverage.","futura":"Modify the process so that appointments are scheduled directly in Beta, ideally within a dedicated section of the legal case file for follow-up appointments, through a form or space available daily from 6:00 a.m. the following day, which can be filled in by field attorneys, coordinators, or any member of the legal team with a Beta user account. This space must contain all the data currently sent in the email format — such as appointment date and time, location, client, event, legal case, etc. — and must also include Beta-specific fields, for example the active team drop-down, so that once the information is submitted by the user, it flows directly into a repository in Beta and is stored there. The information should then be downloadable as a flat file available at 7:00 a.m. every day of the week, so coordinators or those supporting them can work the file, filter and select the day's appointments, and send the assignment by email to the team that will carry them out. Additionally, when an appointment is registered, a notification must be sent to the collaborator's mobile phone, it must appear in their task panel, and Beta must generate daily compliance reports. Finally, at the end of the day, there must be a link between the legal case and the form so that the outcome is reflected accordingly.","gap":"Reduce human error stemming from email communication, manual review, and subsequent entry into Excel or Drive, thereby avoiding omissions or incorrect records. It also makes Legal Guard's resources more efficient by eliminating manual consolidation, download, and distribution tasks, and reduces the operational pressure of delivering reports within tight time windows. By recording appointments directly in Beta, completeness, traceability, security, and data availability are improved, enabling measurement of the operational workload by case, period, or collaborator. Finally, operational risk is reduced, dependency on a single intermediate unit as a single point of failure is eliminated, and attorneys and Legal Guard are freed from time-consuming tasks so they can focus on higher-value work.","sug":"Develop a native scheduling and appointment management module in Beta, with direct registration, automatic consolidation, notifications, reporting, and export capabilities — eliminating email and manual data entry into spreadsheets.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"Automating the appointment scheduling and assignment process in Beta represents a key opportunity to strengthen operational efficiency, reduce manual errors, and improve information traceability. In Colombia, we currently have a hearings report and each member of the legal team schedules meetings with clients or working sessions with authorities directly in their own calendars; however, manually consolidating this information makes daily organization and prioritization difficult. Having a centralized, real-time repository would facilitate operational planning and provide full visibility of hearings and team commitments.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-003":{"tit":"Repeat-offender and criminal-gang file integration","actual":"Repeat-offender and criminal-gang file integration. When any event is generated and identifying data (photograph and name) is available for the detained individuals, an internal search is conducted across emails, drives, and groups to check whether the person being handed over to the authorities is linked to other files or identified as a member of a gang.","futura":"Generate an alert at the moment a name is entered, and have Beta provide information on related files.","gap":"• Improve efficiency for the back-office team in administrative work • Reduce human error, since manual searches of databases can cause valuable information to be overlooked that should be referenced in the file being worked on at the time • Ensure that information is reliable and that we have a complete file.","sug":"Incorporate the Offender functionality into the new complaint management model. Suggests making the CURP field mandatory in the closing report to improve search accuracy.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"It is considered important to incorporate search by identification number within the functionality, since limiting queries solely by the subject's name can produce inaccuracies due to cases of individuals sharing the same name, or situations in which offenders — especially foreign nationals — are not identified by their full names. This would allow us to improve the identification of repeat offenders and gang members.","CL":"Although the future functionality makes sense to us, we understand that the current configuration of the Offender module in Beta facilitates the work, and it would be very interesting to introduce match alerts. Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-004":{"tit":"Availability and location of field attorneys","actual":"There is currently no structured way to view, in real time, the location, availability, and operational progress of field attorneys as they handle events, appointments, and hearings. This information is reported via WhatsApp, making it dependent on manual messages rather than a formal status update within the system.","futura":"Have the platform provide functionality through a button that allows attorneys to report arrival and departure, without the field being open or editable — meaning it could be linked to the clock on mobile devices. Have the system automatically update the status (e.g., \"Available\") when the closing report is submitted.","gap":"Measure the duration of each proceeding and generate a record of those times, enabling data-driven operational decisions.","sug":"Use the volume of activities and the system's historical data to automatically estimate how long it will be before an attorney is available again.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"We have a man-hours table to quantify the estimated time for each judicial and administrative proceeding; it can serve as a reference, but loses accuracy in complex cases involving multiple defendants and multiple defense attorneys, where team availability cannot be controlled due to external factors or travel time between locations.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-005":{"tit":"Internal operational report generation","actual":"Zone coordinators report events with detained individuals and their eligibility for Restorative Agreements via WhatsApp. This information is manually consolidated in a Drive to generate the internal management report \"-3+1\".","futura":"Extract internal statistics directly from the platform without the need to consolidate text reports from WhatsApp.","gap":"Reduce the administrative burden on coordinators and gain agile visibility to support internal operational decision-making.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"Our information is extracted directly from data entered into the platform.","CL":"Although the type of reporting differs, in Chile — at least on our team — we must consult our internal records (Drive) to verify that information is complete. The ideal would be to move to a system that contains all the necessary fields to generate instant reports for the client. Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-006":{"tit":"Agile multimedia evidence upload and integration (Photos)","actual":"Attorneys share photographs of defendants and external evidence through WhatsApp groups (e.g., \"Farderos\") because the mechanisms for uploading this content to the platform (Beta) are slow and cumbersome.","futura":"Improve the platform's mechanisms so that uploading a photo is as fast and intuitive as doing so via WhatsApp.","gap":"Prevent the operation from creating silos of unstructured information outside the system, and centralize visual evidence.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"Increasing the storage capacity for photos and videos in Beta will ensure a more reliable and useful record for offender identification processes. Although full identification of the individuals involved is already available in some cases, strengthening the collection and preservation of audiovisual material will optimize analysis and investigation work, contributing to the dismantling of criminal gangs and networks. It is necessary to allow multiple photos in order to track physical changes; currently only one photo is permitted. This new development would reduce dependence on other team members, such as the video analyst, for verifying the existence of photographs and recordings that could be submitted as supporting evidence in judicial proceedings.","CL":"In Chile, a similar problem exists, as documents such as file copies are shared via email and WhatsApp, with Beta often bypassed as a system where files can be uploaded and downloaded for review. Perhaps what is needed is to mandate and enforce the use of this system so that attorneys can find the files they need. Convergence: Yes","USA":"This functionality may be used by the USA team in the future, but it is not a current request from the USA team. — Optimizing data entry and the user experience is always welcome, but it is not relevant at this stage."}},"MX-007":{"tit":"Internal visibility of the client interface (\"Mirror\")","actual":"The Relevants team has no operational visibility to verify what information or modules each client sees when they log into their Beta session.","futura":"Gain access to a \"mirror\" view that allows the internal team to see the Beta platform exactly as the client counterpart sees it.","gap":"Validate internally that the information shown to the external user is correct and aligns without errors with the progress records in Drive.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations if referring to external units; however, being able to see things as the client sees them is important."}},"MX-008":{"tit":"Automated and self-service reports in Beta","actual":"Metrics reports are assembled manually by cross-referencing data to build tables and presentations, generating a heavy workload and urgent last-minute demands (\"firefighting\").","futura":"A module in Beta where clients can access their automated reports at any time, containing heat maps, charts, and the status of their events.","gap":"Achieve client informational self-service and optimize weekly meetings to focus them purely on legal strategy.","sug":"Suggests systematizing and automating a \"case status sheet\" that summarizes and displays procedural progress in a straightforward way.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"A dashboard has been developed for some clients; however, it is suggested that for Colombia this reporting format be replicated across all accounts in order to standardize information tracking. It is also necessary to define whether the management analysis covers all cases or only those considered strategic, so that management and oversight efforts can be properly focused.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations, but could have some potential use in the USA market as an alternative to the current way reports are delivered to clients. — Evaluate how Discovery reports can address this before moving forward with new development."}},"MX-009":{"tit":"Formal anonymous reporting platform","actual":"Reports of internal crimes or integrity violations by employees are communicated through informal channels, losing official traceability.","futura":"Have a structured, secure, and anonymous platform available for employees to report crimes and misconduct by colleagues.","gap":"Eradicate operational malpractice, protect whistleblowers, and formalize corporate compliance investigations.","sug":"RC: Suggests sharing the form and questions (Google Forms) previously designed by the attorney with Saúl, so they can be incorporated into the configuration of the new tool. IH: Clarifies that the new whistleblowing tool in the process of being contracted will have a dual scope: it will function internally (for employees) and externally (for clients).","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"In Colombia, the anonymous reporting channel for clients and third parties has been lost, which represents a limitation in receiving sensitive and timely information. Additionally, there is no repository to store, organize, and consult this type of information, which hinders its use in investigation and case management processes.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Internally we have HR, and externally clients have HR; this process is normally managed through the client's existing governance structures or HR."}},"MX-010":{"tit":"Dedicated channel for operational improvement ideas","actual":"Field attorneys do not have an adequate or official channel through which to escalate efficiency proposals tailored to their local realities.","futura":"Enable a channel or module dedicated exclusively to collecting operational ideas and suggestions from field staff.","gap":"Surface operational efficiencies directly from field experience, keeping suggestions separate from the complaint workload.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-011":{"tit":"Automated preventive recommendation engine","actual":"Security suggestions currently depend on additional consulting engagements or external audits, without leveraging incident reports to generate early systemic alerts.","futura":"Have the system analyze crime recurrence and intelligence information to automatically issue preventive guidelines or recommendations to the client within their interface.","gap":"Deliver proactive value to the client by suggesting immediate improvements to their security operation in response to detected theft methodologies.","sug":"Suggests configuring logic-based rules in the system using historical data so that recommendations are generated in a fully automated way, without requiring prior manual validation.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"This approach would allow for greater adaptation to each client's specific needs, improving the timeliness of information, supporting decision-making, and enabling the implementation of preventive measures based on identified patterns.","CL":"It would be interesting for the system to cross-reference information to identify not only repeat offenders, but also addresses or locations where a crime is repeatedly committed, for example. Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-012":{"tit":"Legal skills leveling and practical training program","actual":"New attorneys attend hearings without knowing how to conduct themselves or argue before judges and Public Prosecutors, replicating poor practices observed from third parties.","futura":"Create a general knowledge exam through a specific administration process to verify that answers are genuine, covering both criminal procedure and ALTO's own processes and values.","gap":"Identify which collaborators have a low level of knowledge in criminal law as well as in ALTO's processes, since this directly affects the operation — while conversely, a collaborator with extensive knowledge benefits it. Once low-performing collaborators are identified, we can focus on bringing them up to standard, and recognize those who already perform well.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"If replicated in Chile, the idea would be to have criminal litigation courses taught by the company's more experienced attorneys. Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-013":{"tit":"Artificial Intelligence training and integration","actual":"The team invests a large amount of operational time (\"grunt work\") in day-to-day manual tasks, such as drafting legal briefs, reviewing case files, or copying information into Excel tables.","futura":"Provide cross-functional training to all staff on the standardized use of AI, primarily focused on models such as Gemini and NotebookLM.","gap":"Dramatically improve and accelerate the daily work of all staff, enabling them to discover new ways to carry out their tasks and use them correctly.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Although AI does facilitate the drafting of legal briefs, it requires continuous review to avoid errors. As an alternative, it is recommended to work with the continuous improvement team to facilitate the mass creation of standardized complaints and briefs, as has been done in the case of Telefónica Chile theft complaints. Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-014":{"tit":"Assignment notification to the attorney and access to event data","actual":"Legal Guard requests event assignments via WhatsApp and then calls the attorney; the attorney receives an email with brief information and contact details. The meeting clarifies that this email can be delayed by 10 to 30 minutes from the time the case is created in the system.","futura":"Once an event is assigned, Beta must send a direct notification to the collaborator's mobile phone. Additionally, Beta must include a tab within the legal case containing integrated contact details.","gap":"Unify all information exclusively in Beta, avoiding dependence on a workflow split between email on one side and the legal case on the other.","sug":"Send push notifications via an App/WebApp, or alternatively via WhatsApp with a direct link to the system.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"Implementing direct mobile notifications upon event assignment in Beta, together with the integration of contact details within each legal case, represents an important improvement in operational management and provides immediate access to relevant information about the case owner for study and preparation of the judicial proceeding. It should be reviewed whether this alert would apply only to direct attorneys or also to contractors and outsourced personnel.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"This functionality may be used by the USA team in the future, but it is not a current request from the USA team. — USA's current operational workflows do not appear to operationally depend on real-time notification synchronization at that level."}},"MX-015":{"tit":"Drive population with information by state","actual":"As a result of generated events, coordinators extract information from WhatsApp reports and manually populate a Drive file by state.","futura":"Beta must automatically transfer the data entered by collaborators to a Drive file by state, to which the coordination team has access to verify completeness.","gap":"Time savings by eliminating manual data entry, facilitating complex analysis of missing fields, and avoiding information discrepancies by standardizing the data extracted.","sug":"Replace the spreadsheet with a real-time control Dashboard in the system, or test a direct connection between Beta and BigQuery to auto-populate queries and eliminate manual spreadsheets.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"Using the platform as the sole means of updating in Colombia contributes to the centralization of information and reduces the risk of data loss. However, it is necessary to strengthen data quality by encouraging more detailed, specific, and consistent entries; awareness campaigns should be created to make the legal team accountable for the information they provide.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-016":{"tit":"Direct mobile access to Beta","actual":"Beta is accessed via a web link, making its use on attorneys' devices less direct.","futura":"Have Beta available as a direct application on collaborators' devices.","gap":"Greater fluidity and agility in attorneys' use of Beta, better receipt of notifications on mobile devices regarding assignments, tasks, or appointments, and differentiation of web access for coordination teams — orienting it more toward reporting, summaries, and dashboards.","sug":"Evaluate a direct mobile access mode for Beta on corporate Android devices, whether through a WebApp/PWA or a mobile application, complemented by usage training for attorneys.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"Having a mobile application that enables real-time access and information updates would significantly facilitate the team's work, especially in waiting scenarios such as at the URI. This would allow downtime to be used for timely data entry, avoiding task accumulation and reducing delays in case updates.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — It is recommended to prioritize the consolidation and improvement of existing functionality in Beta, rather than introducing parallel platforms or disconnected workflows."}},"MX-017":{"tit":"Outcome reporting (Closing report)","actual":"There is operational duplication: field attorneys are required to write an email with their \"closing report\" as a record and, simultaneously, to enter the same fields in Beta, which causes frustration and low adoption of the tool.","futura":"The attorney will enter the outcome of the assigned task in Beta only. The system will automatically consolidate this information to generate compliance reports.","gap":"Reduction of the administrative burden in the field, elimination of duplicate data entry, and the generation of real operational metrics per collaborator.","sug":"Use the information already entered by the attorney in Beta so the system auto-generates and sends the evidence email (\"closing report\"), reducing operational friction.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"Allowing the system to automatically generate and send a summary with the basic case data the day after it is updated would reduce the team's administrative burden, avoiding manual email drafting and minimizing potential errors or inconsistencies in the information. (This applies to some clients who request these reports the day after a flagrante delicto case.)","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — The functionality already exists in Beta. This appears to be more of an operational training issue."}},"MX-018":{"tit":"Centralized management home panel (Dashboard)","actual":"To handle a new event, the attorney must search for contact details in their email and then separately log into the Beta system to record their work, forcing them to triangulate between platforms.","futura":"Implement a centralized home panel or dashboard in Beta where the collaborator immediately sees their pending events and store contact details.","gap":"Organically drive exclusive use of Beta by centralizing the workflow and speeding up response time to events.","sug":"Create a home screen (dashboard) in the system where the attorney can always see their list of pending tasks and contacts without needing to check their email.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Cases already have a contacts section in Beta. Not relevant to USA operations at this stage."}},"MX-019":{"tit":"Remote event information collection from stores","actual":"The attorney must go in person to the store to request information and gather the event narrative. This occurs because the initial report generated by the store or post-sale team is usually very brief or insufficient for legal proceedings.","futura":"Information collection must be managed remotely through a call center, a web system, or pre-established forms. The client or operator must enter all details exhaustively without requiring the attorney to visit the store.","gap":"Direct time savings from eliminating physical travel and data collection. This recovered time can be invested in legal matters that truly require technical expertise.","sug":"Proposes expanding the operator's (call center or guard's) question protocol so that the initial questionnaire is more comprehensive and able to meet legal needs from the very first contact.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"The future functionality makes sense for Chile. Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-020":{"tit":"Digital generation of complaints to the Public Prosecutor's Office","actual":"Attorneys attend in person at the Public Prosecutor's Office and spend multiple hours in line to open investigation files for minor offenses without a detained suspect. This operational burden is used as justification for not attending more significant trial hearings.","futura":"Open investigation files by entering data through the prosecutors' digital platforms, such as those available in Mexico City or Nuevo León. The system must automatically generate the official complaint with a digital seal.","gap":"Massive man-hour savings, estimated at up to 100 hours per week. This speeds up document delivery to the client for insurance claims and allows attorneys to be reassigned to relevant trials.","sug":"Suggests that the attorney use Google Meet to record their screen while filing a standard complaint on the prosecutor's office portal. This will allow the IT team to observe the process and its requirements in order to evaluate a systems interconnection.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"Standardizing a format for medium- and low-complexity complaints, together with its direct integration with the Attorney General's Office or National Police platforms, represents a relevant opportunity to optimize the filing process. This interconnection would reduce processing times, minimize manual intervention, and streamline complaint submission; it would also contribute to the uniformity of reported information, reducing errors in completion.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-021":{"tit":"Autonomous case status inquiry and accountability","actual":"Case updates are performed manually by sending periodic emails with summaries, images, and attached documents. Clients do not use the Beta platform autonomously and frequently complain about a perceived lack of information.","futura":"Clients log in autonomously and directly to the Beta platform to check the status, history, and everything they need regarding their cases.","gap":"Mitigation of client complaints about lack of updates and visibility. Reduction of the administrative time attorneys spend drafting emails manually.","sug":"Suggests sending an automated email containing only a direct link to the platform, forcing the client to log into the system to view their report. Also proposes integrating Artificial Intelligence to upload meeting agreements, enabling the client to query the AI about their history to validate the work performed.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Already exists in Beta. Client email updates and case status dashboards in Discovery."}},"MX-022":{"tit":"Dynamic reports and dashboards by client","actual":"Results reports by client, where information loaded into Beta can be reported on; the reports are displayed uniformly, always showing the same information.","futura":"The ideal for pulling client reports is to be able to choose which information to display, selecting only what the client requires at a given moment — for example, if a client asks for all simple thefts in Jalisco for the months of June, July, and August where only men were the perpetrators, this information should be visualizable in the dashboard with figures, charts, and heat maps.","gap":"1. It would avoid spending time preparing the corresponding slides; 2. It would provide accurate information that resides only in Beta; 3. Efficiency in delivering information to the client more quickly; 4. Elimination of information delays.","sug":"Add a gender filter. Clarifies that the need to create a structured, graphical dashboard is a system requirement distinct from answering spontaneous numerical queries.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Discovery dashboards have filters available for clients. Configure reports in Discovery together with the BI team. Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-023":{"tit":"Task assignment, follow-up, and traceability","actual":"Task assignment. Tasks and follow-ups are currently assigned via email: 1. the client assigns a task to us by email, 2. we assign that task to the appropriate coordination team, 3. the coordination team assigns the task to the team they select, 4. they return the corresponding response to us, and 5. we share that response with the client. Between 80 and 100 client task emails are received daily and manually forwarded to coordinators. With no centralized record, emails get lost, deadlines are missed, and manual follow-up via WhatsApp or phone calls becomes necessary.","futura":"Ideally all tasks would be assigned directly in Beta so they reach the coordinator, who can then assign them to the appropriate person, with the following features: 1. Constant alerts as reminders when a task has not been completed, so nothing is lost sight of. 2. A record of all activities conducted via email that currently goes untracked. 3. The ability to classify tasks so that a record can be kept by crime type and/or issue involved. Assign tasks directly in Beta to the responsible coordinator. The system must issue constant alerts and reminders for non-compliance, and also classify tasks by crime or issue.","gap":"1. It would help ensure that assigned tasks are carried out more efficiently and consistently, as reminders would prevent colleagues from forgetting them. 2. By having a record by crime type or issue and by store, a count can be maintained to provide a more accurate report to the client.","sug":"Suggests sharing a ticket identifier with the client so they feel the request has been formalized. Recommends naming the process \"client legal service\" or \"client legal consultation,\" avoiding \"advisory\" to prevent conflicts within the system.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Clients do not assign tasks in USA. Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-024":{"tit":"Automated alerts and tagging by criminal gang","actual":"Event alerts arrive by email with general information about the store and the facts. Identification of organized gangs is done by manually reading the narrative.","futura":"Have the system analyze the narrative to identify specific conditions, such as thefts involving 3 or more people or names such as \"Banda de la Morena.\" Upon detection, it must classify the gang name and send a specific alert.","gap":"Better identification and visibility of criminal gangs operating in stores.","sug":"Proposes programming Beta so that, when automatically analyzing and creating the \"legal case\" (Mexico's operation), the system identifies these conditions, adds the label or tag directly to the case, and triggers the alert email.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"This functionality is useful; it will allow the attorney to identify these cases and give them the appropriate attention and follow-up, requesting the physical and material evidence for further action.","CL":"That said, the working teams in Chile have currently configured alerts directly from Gmail to automatically identify gang cases. Adding the label or tag feature is interesting. Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-025":{"tit":"Spontaneous queries and quick counts (e.g., Official Letters)","actual":"The client makes urgent spontaneous queries (e.g., number of official letters processed or thefts in a given year), for which the attorney uses manual Excel databases. The attorney does not use the Beta system for this because they perceive it as not being fully up to date.","futura":"Use the system to quickly filter specific data and obtain exact counts instantly, without needing to build a complete graphical dashboard.","gap":"Achieve immediate response times to client requests. Eliminate dependency on manually maintained and built Excel spreadsheets.","sug":"Suggests using Beta's Viewer functionality to filter cases by crime type, sector, or client, and download the results directly to Excel. Encourages the attorney to try this tool.","obs":{"MX":"Based on the IT proposal, we would add that it is necessary to build the various filter configurations required by the Mexico legal team — including those already incorporated or established in the dashboards we have in Loker as pilots, specifically the Agreements dashboard and the Home Depot Legal Management dashboard.","CO":"Leveraging the information already consolidated in the platform is an opportunity to review each client's needs, as they request this information spontaneously with little response time. It is essential that this information be adapted to the specific needs of each client and sector, avoiding the rigidity of a single standard format that does not account for operational particularities. This approach would improve response agility and reduce manual consolidation time.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"This functionality may be used by the USA team in the future, but it is not a current request from the USA team. — If information were entered in Alliance instead of Excel files, Alliance would stay up to date. The functionality already exists in Alliance."}},"MX-026":{"tit":"Sub-classification of new operational incidents (Street Vendors and Tents)","actual":"Recurring and critical operational issues at Walmart, such as street vendor commerce (\"ambulantes\") or \"gaming tents\" (illegal casinos), do not exist in Beta's catalog. These incidents are recorded under generic labels such as \"unlawful entry\" or \"other,\" preventing a quick count.","futura":"Expand Beta's catalog by creating sub-classifications or specific drop-down fields to record the exact nature of these real client problems.","gap":"Real visibility and traceability of these specific operational issues in the system. Ability to provide clients with accurate and precise statistics when required.","sug":"Submit via ticket.","obs":{"MX":"Regarding this gap, we identified that perhaps our initial description of the current state and what we want for the future is inaccurate, as we were able to conclude that the section for the catalog already exists, and that perhaps what is missing is the option for \"street vendor\" or \"gaming tent.\" We estimate that by generating a ticket with an adequate description, or even through a conversation with IT, we can get to what we need.","CO":"Not all advisory work corresponds to acts constituting a criminal offense. Currently, work such as following up on street vendors, visiting scrapyards, or other preventive or verification tasks is not reflected in the platform, which limits the client's visibility of the work performed in the field. It is limited to delivering a report from the team so the client has context on the activities carried out on site.","CL":"Very local issue. Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — The ability to add incident types already exists in Alliance."}},"MX-027":{"tit":"Case file integration checklist","actual":"In Beta, only general statuses are mentioned, such as Case File Integration or Initial Stage. Specific proceedings are recorded as comments or \"checkpoints\" in the log, requiring review of long histories to verify what has been completed. Only the following statuses are listed: Case File Integration, Initial Stage, Intermediate Stage, Trial Stage, Appeals Stage, Concluded, Cancelled.","futura":"Case file integration. Add a display of the proceedings that a file must have in order to be fully integrated: Complaint, Prosecution Brief, Accreditation, Witnesses, Videos, Merchandise Recovery *.","gap":"Total proceedings per file. Case file integration and better outcomes when individuals are arrested in a separate file. Less time to request arrest warrants.","sug":"Notes that although \"tags\" are currently used in the log, a better summary is needed because the current display requires re-analyzing the entire case constantly.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"Should be evaluated once Beta is fully implemented for Colombia.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Exception reports through Insights would allow showing if a case is missing something specific, as well as the dates and times when something changed or was completed."}},"MX-028":{"tit":"Appointment report and direct entry","actual":"When a proceeding is carried out, the appointment report and its outcomes are handled by sending emails to Legal Guard. In Beta, only \"Touchpoints\" exist, but they do not clearly define what was done or whether the requested action was fulfilled.","futura":"Appointment reporting. Currently, once a previously scheduled proceeding is completed, the outcome must be sent by email. It is required that information be loaded directly in Beta into each assigned case, where it can be reviewed more quickly and efficiently. Currently only Touchpoints are available, but they do not define what was done or whether what was requested was fulfilled.","gap":"Information is loaded directly in Beta, making it more efficient to search for outcomes related to case file integration, reducing email use, and increasing work on the Beta platform.","sug":"Clarifies that the technical model in Beta converts appointments into assigned tasks, so that when they are completed on site, the compliance record is automatically generated.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Touchpoints have 2 parts: the label and the comment. The comment should already clearly define what was done, according to the user's account. Touchpoints can also generate emails on the same day or at the end of the week when completed."}},"MX-029":{"tit":"Notifications for merchandise recovery","actual":"Merchandise recovery is a parallel process in which the responsible area sends a monthly Excel file with pending items.","futura":"Implement a scheduled notification or alert in the system indicating when merchandise has not been recovered within the estimated time.","gap":"Enables verification with the team of the reasons for delays, taking the necessary measures, avoiding backlogs, and recovering merchandise quickly and in a timely manner.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-030":{"tit":"Management workflow for postponed or cancelled appointments","actual":"If a scheduled appointment cannot take place due to an unforeseen event, Beta has no functionality to manage it. The attorney must search through email history to find out what happened to the failed proceeding.","futura":"Create a workflow in the system that allows reporting whether an appointment was postponed, cancelled, or rescheduled, with the reasons justified directly in the platform.","gap":"Effective control and follow-up of appointments that are not carried out, avoiding information gaps without having to filter through email inboxes.","sug":"Confirms that the current system has a gap for managing failed appointments and proposes drafting and reviewing a new technological workflow to channel these cases.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"This is addressed through the hearing and activity scheduling feature, in which the observation was made.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — If touchpoints are scheduled, the date can be updated. If tasks are scheduled, the date can be updated. Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-031":{"tit":"Mass management and assignment interface for coordinators","actual":"The assignment flow in the system is case by case. The coordinator must enter event by event to assign the daily volume of appointments to their attorneys.","futura":"Implement a general management interface that consolidates tasks and facilitates assignment to team members.","gap":"Helps the coordinator clearly ensure and visualize the workload and task distribution across the different members of the team.","sug":"Acknowledges that no general collaborator-workload management interface exists, and recommends reviewing functionally how the team would use it before implementing it.","obs":{"MX":"Adds an additional comment despite the proposal having been initiated by the country: In order not to lose sight of the comment regarding this gap, we decided to put it on record at this time — specifically, what we identified here is that the description or definition of what we want for the future fell short in terms of understanding, since what we are referring to is assigning by tasks or appointments for the day, where two or more may be for the same assignee and the coordinator would not necessarily have to enter each case individually, but rather by execution date with the possibility of one or more appointments or tasks per assignee.","CO":"This is handled through the call center or the judicial-dependency team.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-032":{"tit":"Reordering of the event-creation flow","actual":"The system requires filling in fields in the following order: 1. Country/Account, 2. Event category, 3. Location (store), 4. Date and time, 5. Event description, and additional sections. Going back clears the information already entered. Additionally, requiring classification of the offense before hearing the facts creates inefficiency and errors.","futura":"Change the order to: 1. Country/Account, 2. Location (store), 3. Event description, 4. Date and time, 5. Event category (Offense), and then additional sections. The description must come first so that the correct offense classification can be derived from it.","gap":"Streamlines the intake of advisory calls and ensures correct classification of reports. Prevents data loss when navigating back through the form.","sug":"Submit via ticket.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-033":{"tit":"Account and store search in event creation","actual":"The system currently requires entering the exact store name (e.g., \"Hennes & Mauritz\" instead of H&M). Clients often provide imprecise information or refer to stores by area (e.g., \"Coppel Iztapalapa\"). Operators depend on an external directory to look up addresses and then enter them into the system.","futura":"Provide autocomplete to easily locate units and generate a more complete store finder where searches can be performed by entering parameters such as three letters or a city.","gap":"Minimize client hold time while locating their unit, avoiding frustration during the call.","sug":"Expand the requirement to build a far more complete, efficient, and robust store finder integrated into event creation, one that does not depend on a separate directory and supports cross-parameter searches.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"The way incidents are reported in Chile differs from the reality in Mexico. Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — While this specific problem is not relevant to USA, IT must allow partial search results and not only exact matches. This is a basic UX requirement."}},"MX-034":{"tit":"Direct recording of authority-issued appointments","actual":"Currently a standard form is generated for appointments received from the authority; that information is then manually re-entered, duplicating it in an appointment log (Excel/Drive).","futura":"Be able to record any appointment directly in Beta, with a native section for entering the data in one click, and allow downloading that information without generating intermediate forms or sending duplicate emails.","gap":"Concentrates time on advisory intake. Eliminates manual operational steps and duplicate data entry.","sug":"Automate the process so the system reads authority email information directly, or create a process with no intermediate steps.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"This was already noted under a similar point.","CL":"We already have this. Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-035":{"tit":"Real-time incident log for event assignment","actual":"In the current process, the operator takes the advisory call and must manually record the information in an external \"incident log\" (spreadsheet) and keep it updated. Coordinators use this spreadsheet to see which event has been generated and assign an attorney. In Legacy this was visible in real time.","futura":"Have a native section with a view of generated events (drafts or in progress), allowing the different coordinators to immediately see the state or municipality so they can assign their team members to the various events.","gap":"Efficiency in event response. Completely replaces double-entry in the external Excel incident log.","sug":"The incident spreadsheet should be generated automatically by the system as soon as an event is created, without the operator having to tabulate that information manually.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"A data sheet is available.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-036":{"tit":"Global visibility and editing of draft events","actual":"The current operator can only view in the call center the draft events they themselves created. If the computer shuts down, the internet fails, or there is a shift change, other colleagues cannot view or edit the draft to continue follow-up.","futura":"Be able to view and edit draft events from a user account different from the one that created them, allowing any colleague to complete them to ensure proper follow-up.","gap":"Prevents events from falling through the cracks — which could lead to client complaints — and facilitates recovery work in emergencies or technical failures.","sug":"Add two filters to the Call Center screen: one to separate the view between draft and completed events, and another to show \"my events\" or \"everyone's events.\" TICKET","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"The way incidents are reported in Chile differs from the reality in Mexico. Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. The issue stems from IT user-management decisions."}},"MX-037":{"tit":"Partial draft saving in the initial flow","actual":"The operator is required to complete all initial steps of the flow (including date/time and classification) before being able to press \"save draft\" and unlock the evidence or persons sections.","futura":"Allow saving the event partially at an early stage, requiring only the initial mandatory fields (country, store, and description).","gap":"Protects information against human errors, dropped calls, or the need to attend a second line. Allows coordinators to receive preliminary information without waiting for full data entry.","sug":"Allow saving with a \"pending completion\" status and streamline the flow so the description and case ID are sent directly to the attorney so they can begin working in parallel.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-038":{"tit":"Decoupling attorney assignment from event closure","actual":"The operator is required to wait for the coordinator to assign and notify the attorney before being able to finish recording the event from their advisory call, which prevents them from taking new calls.","futura":"Attorney assignment must be a process independent from the operator's ticket entry in the Call Center.","gap":"Time savings for the operator. Allows them to become available quickly after recording the incident and prevents bottlenecks when new emergency calls come in.","sug":"Include attorney assignment as a separate flow within event creation, requiring the coordinator to assign without blocking the operator.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-039":{"tit":"Repeat-Offender Alerts","actual":"No automated system currently exists. A photo, name, and data of the detained person are sent to a WhatsApp group, and a team manually searches for name matches in an Excel/Drive list of persons of interest.","futura":"Repeat-Offender Alerts: we would like to have a feature that issues real-time alerts about repeat offenders, triggered the moment any user loads the name of the person involved — that is, Beta should analyze the loaded name and automatically cross-reference it against all other names it has on file as persons of interest, and if a match is found, issue an alert configured for certain users (e.g., coordinators, account-specialist attorneys, and others) indicating that the person has a prior offense record, detailing the case identification data (client, event number, legal case, offense, etc.), the number of matches found, and the details of each one, including photos of the person of interest that may have been uploaded in previous cases. ENHANCED: Develop a feature that, at the moment any person of interest's name is loaded, cross-references the information in real time against the entire database (persons of interest, witnesses, guards, or others) and issues targeted alerts to specific users. RELATED TO INTELLIGENCE.","gap":"Centralization and security of information, efficiency by eliminating manual searches, critical strengthening for pre-trial detention in investigation files, and generation of a major commercial competitive advantage.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"This was already addressed under a similar point about handling photos and videos.","CL":"In any case, Chile currently does have a process that calculates recidivism and delivers it in report form. The interesting opportunity would be to incorporate it as part of the Beta interface. Convergence: Yes","USA":"This closely aligns with the USA request for an Offender-based model. — The functionality is similar to the Offender-based model; however, it is based on client-side incident reporting, as opposed to the internal case-data analysis that was requested. Not relevant to USA operations due to how information is received from clients."}},"MX-040":{"tit":"3-Level Strategy","actual":"Classification and case control by strategic impact level (1, 2, or 3, with or without a detained person) is performed manually using an Excel file or the client's external log.","futura":"3-Level Strategy: Level 1 AR, and alerts for case-processing deadline milestones // link to strategy objectives //","gap":"Eliminates dependence on external manual logs and ensures compliance with the criminal strategy directly from the official platform.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Appears to be centered on regional operational practices."}},"MX-041":{"tit":"AI in Beta: Gemini: judicial strategy skill","actual":"The attorney downloads case documentation (e.g., complaints) from the system and manually uploads it to a generic external AI tool (Gemini), which is then asked to act as defense or prosecuting counsel to suggest strategies.","futura":"Have the system itself directly analyze all loaded case information and suggest evidentiary steps (e.g., request C5, forensic evaluator) based on the applicable Criminal Code or current protocols.","gap":"Saves operational time, supplements potential gaps in tactical knowledge among local attorneys, and standardizes defense quality nationwide.","sug":"Rather than a generic \"AI in Beta,\" build a specific legal-strategy advisory agent iteratively trained on the legal matrix.","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"Incorporating analysis and information-support tools would contribute significantly to decision-making by providing a more structured and timely view of cases. However, these solutions must be understood as support for the process and not as a replacement for professional judgment. Accordingly, it remains essential that the attorney conduct a substantive analysis of each case and determine the most appropriate strategy, ensuring that legal decisions are built on experience, context, and applicable law.","CL":"It would be very useful in managing our cases. In general, we do not usually use this tool, at least not for drafting our complaints — we know how to prepare them and what steps are needed for each type of offense — but it would save time given the volume of cases we handle. Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. AI should not perform the work of a legal team member. Excessive reliance on AI would erode ALTO's brand image as a subject-matter expert."}},"MX-042":{"tit":"Reparatory Agreements","actual":"Detailed management (amount deposited, amount stolen, perishables) is handled in an external Google Drive because no fields exist in Beta. Supporting documents such as deposit vouchers and PDF agreements live as lost attachments in email chains.","futura":"Create native transactional capture fields in the system and enable vouchers and evidentiary documentation to be attached directly to the case profile.","gap":"Centralizes confidential and financial information. Eliminates time wasted searching for vouchers in email when the client requests them.","sug":"Submit via ticket.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Incidents and cases can already have attachments. Fields can be updated through IT."}},"MX-043":{"tit":"Legal Briefs","actual":"Documents such as complaints, formal accusations, and motions to the Public Prosecutor's Office are assembled by manually copying, pasting, and adapting text.","futura":"An automatic brief-generation system in Beta that maintains a nationally standardized structure while customizing the addressee authority and substantive legal grounds depending on the state.","gap":"Significantly reduces attorneys' drafting time and ensures an identical, standardized quality of output for clients across the country.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"This proposal aligns with suggestions made in Colombia aimed at standardizing procedural document formats and templates. Implementing unified templates and structures can contribute significantly to optimizing attorney time, reducing repetitive tasks, and facilitating document preparation.","CL":"AI tools can be used to facilitate automatic drafting. Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"MX-044":{"tit":"Timeline Report","actual":"The time required to complete each phase of the criminal process or to recover merchandise is not measured systematically. No active alerts exist for case lifecycle management.","futura":"Dashboards with traffic-light indicators or parameters that measure SLA timeliness (e.g., maximum 12 hours to file a complaint with a detained person) and warn whether the case is in green, yellow, or red status.","gap":"Enables proactive action before a process or piece of merchandise \"goes critical,\" and gives management visibility into potential bottlenecks by area.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. SLA timelines would differ across USA jurisdictions and depend on external factors. Not recommended."}},"MX-045":{"tit":"Dashboard","actual":"The analysis report and charts must be built manually by pulling data sheets and taking them to Looker, or by asking Gemini to structure the comparative information.","futura":"Native dynamic visualizations in the system that generate time-based comparisons (e.g., January vs. February), gender segmentation, and heat maps to detect organized crime gang activity.","gap":"Fully automates the workload of creating executive client reports and facilitates strategic decision-making.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"This is already built and was noted under a previous item.","CL":"Notwithstanding that it is currently addressed through dashboards built by the Continuous Improvement team. Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. This is already managed through Discovery reports. Create a ticket to the BI team to automate it."}},"MX-046":{"tit":"Field attorney assignment board","actual":"Field attorney assignment is done manually by the coordinator through handwritten notes, memory, or a desktop tool, causing geographically inefficient overlaps.","futura":"Incorporate a visual map or workload-and-schedule board that suggests assignments based on calendar availability and geographic proximity, showing available attorneys in green/red.","gap":"Optimizes attorney travel time in the field and eliminates the bias and logistical errors caused by reliance on the coordinator's memory.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Similar to row 32. Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Specific to a regional operation. Assignments are already in Beta; create a Discovery dashboard to visualize them."}},"MX-047":{"tit":"Service Attendance Certificates","actual":"When visiting a store or attending the Public Prosecutor's Office, the attorney fills out a paper document with a pen, has it signed and stamped, scans it, and sends it by email as a PDF.","futura":"A mobile application or feature where the client or witness signs digitally on screen, indexing the certificate or PDF immediately to the event.","gap":"Digitizes the record, provides immediate traceability of client service, and makes evidence available to refute false claims of poor service.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — It is recommended to prioritize the consolidation and improvement of existing Beta functionality rather than introducing parallel platforms or disconnected flows."}},"MX-048":{"tit":"Assignment and update trend analysis","actual":"When an attorney complains about their workload, up to 2 or 3 days are spent manually reviewing WhatsApp histories, assignment photos, and emails to reconstruct the work performed.","futura":"An analytics tool that historically calculates and visualizes what percentage of total assignments was covered by each attorney (e.g., 75% Pedro, 2% Juan).","gap":"Ensures equity in operational distribution and generates quick documentary evidence to defend against potential labor claims or resignations.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"The information is currently in the database and the existing fields in Beta allow the analysis to be performed. Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Touchpoints, case assignments, and Discovery / Insights dashboards already show this automatically. This does not constitute new development."}},"MX-049":{"tit":"Exclusive fields for Walmart log report","actual":"Weekly, a flat file is downloaded, separated, and manually processed in Excel (with cross-references from other tools) to populate information required by the client that does not exist in Beta (minor, self-recoverable, store area, etc.).","futura":"Add these exclusive, customized fields to the client's case profiles in Beta so that the information is consolidated in the system from the start.","gap":"Completely eliminates the weekly manual Excel data-cross process and reduces reporting errors for the corporate client.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Responds to a local need in Mexico. Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Region- and client-specific: Not relevant to USA operations. New fields can be added via ticket."}},"MX-050":{"tit":"Agreements dashboard","actual":"Reports are built by copying information from an external repository into an Excel template and then pasting it into a final presentation. (It was clarified in the meeting that this is the same as \"Reparatory Agreements\".)","futura":"Centralization of agreement data visualization within the platform, eliminating duplication.","gap":"Reduction of operational steps (same benefits as Reparatory Agreements).","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Request standardized report generation from the BI team."}},"MX-051":{"tit":"Deadline tracking (Milestone alerts)","actual":"Monitoring compliance with the specific actions required at each case level (e.g., 45-day deadline to sign an agreement) is reactive and manual.","futura":"An automatic procedural alert system that triggers notifications indicating when a deadline has passed and the defined procedural objective has not been met.","gap":"Traceability of legal milestone compliance for each type of case cluster.","sug":"Use the Insights functionality, which automatically detects when a legal milestone or document is missing within a given timeframe and notifies via dashboards or alerts.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"Implementing a tracking and control system with traffic-light indicators would significantly improve process management by clearly identifying cases that have not been reviewed within a given period or that show no procedural progress. This type of tool would facilitate prioritization of actions within the team or among account attorneys, ensuring tighter control over the status of each case.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. This sounds like an Insights feature."}},"MX-052":{"tit":"Automatic reminder of operational protocols","actual":"Standardized corporate protocols (e.g., rules for gambling-tent incidents) are sent manually by email to attorneys. Given high turnover, the client has to re-explain everything each time a different attorney or auditor is involved.","futura":"When an event is assigned, the system should deliver an \"executive summary\" with the latest status and notify the assignee on screen of the mandatory protocol steps they must follow.","gap":"Reduces service complaints by 80%, eliminates erroneous or inconsistent interpretations of the protocol by different coordinators, and improves satisfaction.","sug":"Consider that the client or ALTO may have an associated procedure that must be executed when certain conditions are met; at minimum, the system should remind users of this.","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. This appears to be a regional operational matter."}},"MX-053":{"tit":"Property Accreditation (Inventory matching)","actual":"Manual discrepancies and mismatches occur because the items the attorney describes in the accreditation brief do not match those loaded in the system or in the initial ticket.","futura":"An intelligent feature or \"switch\" that analyzes, reads, and matches the items detailed in the accreditation against the inventory already uploaded to the database.","gap":"Prevention of operational errors before the Public Prosecutor's Office and full elimination of time wasted on merchandise mismatches.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CO":"Currently, some clients do not have a defined product list, which leads the team to create records in a non-standardized way. This directly affects the ability to generate reliable statistics, making it impossible to precisely identify the most frequently stolen products or the highest-risk sections within the store. Consequently, it limits the ability to design targeted and effective prevention plans. It is therefore necessary to establish standardized product catalogs to ensure consistency in record-keeping and enable more robust analysis for decision-making.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. This appears to be a data-entry issue, either on the user's side or because the system does not allow the correct information to be entered."}},"CL-004":{"tit":"Automated generation of legal briefs and standard documents","actual":"The preparation of legal briefs and standard documents — including complaints, mass reports, witness summonses, communications, institutional emails, presentations, and other recurring formats — is currently done manually. Users retrieve templates stored on their devices or drives, copy data from events, investigative files, police reports, court rulings, or other sources, and manually fill in fields such as the name of the attorney in charge, RUT, RIT, RUC, client details, address, and other information that already exists in the system. This generates rework, inconsistencies, errors, user dependency, and a high time investment in tasks that could be automated.","futura":"Automated generation of legal briefs and standard documents must be implemented through smart templates that auto-populate data directly from the system (Alliance/Beta), associated drives, or available information sources. This includes complaints by offense type with complete case data — witness names and IDs, responsible attorneys' details, RIT, RUC, RUT —, mass reports tailored by client and offense, witness summonses generated from the database, settlement or conviction notices in PDF format, institutional emails, and presentations. The use of artificial intelligence could enhance the extraction of background information from police reports, court rulings, or investigative files, reducing manual intervention and ensuring documentary consistency.","gap":"Drastically reduces the time spent on manual preparation of recurring briefs and documents, eliminates rework, and minimizes the risk of errors and inconsistencies caused by manually copying data. Frees up the legal team's operational capacity for higher-value tasks, ensuring greater documentary consistency and faster response times.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"Regarding this gap, we consider it important to note that for briefs, these will need to be adapted to a portfolio for each country, within the general function of the platform designed for this purpose.","CO":"Automating the organization and generation of documents allows formats and data to be standardized, minimizes errors associated with manual management, and optimizes operational time by linking information directly to each client.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Attachments can be added to cases, incidents, and touchpoints within Beta. Storing this information outside of Alliance poses data security risks, and syncing the system with external repositories is discouraged."}},"CL-009":{"tit":"Automation of instructions, tasks, and operational records","actual":"Instructions associated with rescheduled hearings must be rewritten manually each time, with no way to automatically retrieve the original instruction linked to the event. Once tasks are created in the legal workflow, they cannot be edited, forcing workarounds or additional records. Witness attendance at trial hearings is not tracked within the platform and is managed through external channels. Additionally, low-priority cases assigned to attorneys in the SPPE unit must be manually reviewed and entered one by one into a drive — a repetitive process dependent on the coordinator's available time, prone to delays and backlog.","futura":"When a hearing is rescheduled, the original associated instruction must be retrievable and automatically generated for the new date, without needing to be rewritten. Tasks created in the legal workflow must be editable once generated. Furthermore, a mechanism — such as a button or enabled field — must be incorporated into the trial hearing task to allow the attorney to record each witness's attendance or absence, with the option to justify non-appearance. Finally, the tracking of low-priority cases must be automated, generating a spreadsheet organized by responsible attorney without requiring manual daily download or data entry.","gap":"Reduces the recurring operational burden associated with instructions, records, and task tracking, eliminating repeated drafting of instructions for rescheduled hearings and manual entry of low-priority cases. Improves witness attendance traceability and legal workflow flexibility, reducing the risk of backlog, delays, and errors from incomplete records.","sug":"Partially resolved in Beta","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this gap for Mexico — we are fine with adding it for us; we even consider that it partially overlaps with one already described for Mexico.","CO":"This functionality will be useful once access to BETA is available, as it will allow hearing dates to be rescheduled efficiently, saving time and facilitating timely information updates.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Beta already has structured operational workflows. Examples are needed to evaluate this request in greater detail."}},"CL-011":{"tit":"Operational data consolidation for management reporting","actual":"Operational reports sent to clients such as Mall Plaza require consolidating information from at least two different sources: the legal spreadsheet — which identifies closed events with no processing due to missing information — and the hearings spreadsheet — which shows events under management and events with associated legal activity. This consolidation process is done manually, consuming time and creating risk of inconsistencies between sources.","futura":"A tool is needed to consolidate in one place the operational and legal information required to generate client reports, integrating data from closed events, events under management, and associated legal activity. The report must be able to be generated automatically or semi-automatically, reducing dependence on multiple spreadsheets and manual intervention in its preparation.","gap":"Reduces the time spent manually consolidating information from multiple sources, lowers the risk of inconsistencies in client reports, and enables faster and more reliable report generation. Improves the quality of service delivered to clients and frees up attorney time for higher-value legal tasks.","sug":"In Beta, data spreadsheets will be generated from the Datalake; therefore, the sources needed for report generation can be downloaded at any time.","obs":{"MX":"We believe this overlaps with a gap already described for Mexico, in lines 23 and 46.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Beta already has automated Discovery reports. Examples are needed to evaluate this request in greater detail."}},"CL-013":{"tit":"Automated generation of reports, summaries, and client communications","actual":"The preparation of communications, reports, PPT presentations, and client reports is done entirely manually, consolidating information from multiple sources such as Alliance, Beta, drives, Excel files, CCTV records, and field-gathered data. This includes detention-hearing outcome communications — completed in PowerPoint case by case —, ACD communications to inform clients of detention-hearing results, semi-annual store visit reports for Falabella with local evaluation criteria, SCP reports prepared manually from images and deadlines extracted case by case from Beta, security reports for clients such as Express 400 that require re-entering information already recorded in Beta, and reports on retrieved videos and entered events that must be built manually for submission. In every case, the process is highly time-consuming, generates rework, and creates strong user dependency.","futura":"Automatic generation of reports, summaries, and client communications must be implemented based on information already recorded in Beta, Alliance, drives, or other sources. Through structured templates or modules — including a task module in Beta for store visits — the system should allow ready-to-send documents to be generated with up-to-date data, relevant groupings by event type, band, or category, and minimal manual intervention, enabling automatic delivery to the corresponding recipients.","gap":"Significantly reduces the time invested in manually preparing client reports and summaries, eliminating rework and the re-entry of information already available in the system. Improves the consistency and timeliness of communications, reduces user dependency, and enables reporting capacity to scale without increasing the team's operational workload.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We believe this gap is already described for Mexico, with a different description but the same objective and approach.","CO":"This implementation of automated reports is very useful — process status, successful outcomes. Part of it is already built in Colombia; however, we are still tied to organizing reports in Excel and PPT to share information with clients.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Beta already has automated Discovery reports. Examples are needed to evaluate this request in greater detail."}},"CL-014":{"tit":"Historical repository and data consolidation for legal reporting","actual":"The information needed for legal and client reporting is spread across multiple legal spreadsheets, drives, Legacy files, and other external sources, with no single historical consolidation. Working with complete data requires manually downloading and cross-referencing multiple spreadsheets. For clients such as CGE, some information must be extracted from drives or from Legacy because the system does not contain all the data required to manage the reporting.","futura":"A single historical file or repository is needed that consolidates legal cases from at least 2016 to the current year, eliminating the need to download and cross-reference multiple spreadsheets. For clients such as CGE, the goal is to move toward having all information available directly in the system, simplifying the reporting process and reducing dependence on external sources or Legacy.","gap":"Centralizes the legal case history in a single source, eliminating the need to cross-reference multiple spreadsheets and reducing report preparation time. Improves the consistency and completeness of information available for clients and for internal management, reducing dependence on external sources and Legacy files.","sug":"This can be partially resolved with the Datalake. Older information not loaded into Legacy needs to be uploaded. Information that does not exist in Alliance must be incorporated.","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"As mentioned earlier, it is necessary to have a unified and historical client report that consolidates information related to legal outcomes, number of cases, and other relevant indicators for management and follow-up.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Beta already has automated Discovery reports. Examples are needed to evaluate this request in greater detail."}},"CL-025":{"tit":"Operational alerts for priority events and missing information","actual":"Priority events or alerts with incomplete or missing background information — such as high-priority Walmart client events — currently require manually drafting emails or WhatsApp messages to request the information from the client or relevant person in charge. This process depends on the user's availability and time, creating a risk of delays in the management of critical cases.","futura":"The system must automatically detect priority events or alerts with incomplete background information and generate a direct alert to the coordinating attorney or responsible party, without requiring prior manual intervention. This would allow missing information to be gathered in a timely manner, reducing response times in high-priority cases.","gap":"Improves reaction time for high-priority events with incomplete background information, reducing dependence on individual user availability to manually draft and send requests. Decreases the risk of delays in managing critical cases and ensures that the responsible team is notified immediately and systematically.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this gap for Mexico — we are fine with adding it for us.","CO":"This suggestion has already been raised in a similar point regarding alerts or case reports for clients.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Insights already exist within Discovery."}},"CL-010":{"tit":"Automation of operational requests and alerts","actual":"Event entry alerts are sent to all users with no option to segment them by type, making it difficult to quickly identify cases relevant to each unit. Requests for missing background information are handled manually: the coordinator or TJ enters each event into a requests drive, assigns it individually to the corresponding technician by client, and then sends an email or WhatsApp message — also manually — to request the pending information. This process depends on the responsible person's available time and leads to a backlog of requests and delays. Additionally, there are no automatic alerts for outdated cases with a complaint filed and an identified defendant that have had no activity for months.","futura":"Event entry alerts must be configurable by type — criminal activity, discharges, and others — so that each user receives only the alerts relevant to their unit or profile. When an event with missing background information is detected, the request must be automatically generated, recorded in the corresponding drive, and assigned to the responsible technician by client. An email or WhatsApp message must also be sent automatically to the person in charge requesting the missing information. Additionally, automatic alerts must be implemented for the responsible attorney when a case with a complaint filed and an identified defendant has had no activity for more than six months, and a periodic report of active cases open for more than one year with no registered outcome must be generated.","gap":"Reduces the manual burden in managing alerts and background information requests, ensuring each user receives only the information relevant to their unit. Improves response timeliness for cases with missing information and enables proactive detection of inactive cases with a complaint filed, reducing the risk of critical cases going without timely follow-up.","sug":"There is an event attention management issue, and another is the dependence on email or other notification mechanisms — shouldn't we work on having a panel that lets each user see what is relevant to them?","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"We have Insights that remind us which data is pending update for each case and which attorney has not updated the event — this is tied to the need for a traffic-light report to manage all strategic cases.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Beta already has automated Discovery reports. Examples are needed to evaluate this request in greater detail."}},"CL-015":{"tit":"Export and customization of operational reports","actual":"Obtaining operational reports and lists is done through dashboards or Excel spreadsheets that are extensive, heavy, and poorly tailored to the user's specific needs. The complaints list, for example, can only be filtered within the platform, which is cumbersome compared to working directly in Excel. General spreadsheets contain large volumes of data that are mostly not required for the immediate task, demanding download time and making it difficult to work with the relevant information.","futura":"The ability to export operational lists and reports — such as the complaints history — to Excel spreadsheets with relevant fields such as date, folio, complainant, and client must be incorporated. Additionally, an automatic reports module within Beta is needed with customizable formats, including configurable columns, data, and tabs according to the user's or client's needs, reducing the download of unnecessary information.","gap":"Improves efficiency in operational data analysis by allowing lists to be exported with the relevant fields for each task, eliminating the need to work with heavy, poorly segmented spreadsheets. Report customization reduces the download of unnecessary information and adapts the system to the real needs of each user or client.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Beta already has automated Discovery reports. Examples are needed to evaluate this request in greater detail."}},"CL-016":{"tit":"Management dashboards and executive visualization for clients","actual":"A panel exists for the CGE client in Alliance, created to allow the client to view key management indicators in real time. However, the panel does not incorporate all relevant elements, lacks segmentation by zone or CGE type, and does not adequately reflect information on complaints and reports. Additionally, data updates experience delays, so the client does not access figures in real time.","futura":"The CGE client's management panel must be expanded to incorporate more relevant indicators, with segmentation by zone or CGE type and a specific breakdown of complaints and reports. A mechanism must also be implemented to update information more quickly and closer to real time, so that the client has an updated and comprehensive view of the management.","gap":"Strengthens the client relationship by offering a more complete, segmented, and up-to-date view of the management, improving transparency and trust in the service. Reduces the need for supplementary manual reports and allows the client to make decisions with more timely and accurate information.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We believe this gap overlaps with the one described in lines 08 and 09 for Mexico.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Beta already has automated Discovery reports. Examples are needed to evaluate this request in greater detail."}},"CL-018":{"tit":"Documentary automation associated with reports, complaints, and SIAU management","actual":"Certain documents and data used in reporting, complaints, and SIAU management must be handled manually and repetitively. Complaints downloadable from the system display the office's old address, with no way to update it automatically. Obtaining documents or files from SIAU is a slow process that requires constant follow-up and immediate download to avoid system errors. The available complaints correspond only to the theft type in a generic format, without adapting to the specific offense or incorporating the descriptive information already existing in the system.","futura":"Documentary management related to reporting and legal processing must be automated. Complaints must be able to be automatically generated associated with the reported offense, incorporating the office's updated address and drawing on the event classification and the facts described by the client as a source, with potential support from generative technology for drafting the statement of facts. The process of obtaining documents from SIAU must be systematized by evaluating the use of an AI procurator that performs the process autonomously and in a structured manner.","gap":"Improves the quality and currency of generated documents, eliminating recurring errors such as outdated data in complaints and reducing the manual burden associated with obtaining documents from SIAU. Enables complaints to be generated tailored to the specific offense using information from the system, increasing documentary consistency and freeing up legal team time.","sug":"Current state and future state do not align.","obs":{"MX":"We consider this gap to overlap with at least two gaps from Mexico in terms of objective and approach, differing only in description; we therefore estimate it can be cross-cutting.","CO":"This matter has been mentioned in another observation.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Not part of the USA operational workflow."}},"CL-020":{"tit":"Normalization and cleansing of master data for individuals, parties, and witnesses","actual":"Information on individuals, defendants, witnesses, complainants, collaborators, and client contacts is currently incomplete, duplicated, outdated, or incorrectly written across different sources. When searching for a defendant by RUT, the system returns multiple records with capitalization variations. Witness and complainant data often arrive from the stores without a RUT or full name. The contact database for clients — such as Walmart — is frequently outdated, making it difficult to send summonses. In internal crime events with more than one person involved, the system does not allow the type of collaborator or colluding client to be correctly distinguished. Additionally, there is no visual indicator to easily identify whether a witness no longer works at the store or has been transferred.","futura":"Centralized, normalized databases of individuals, witnesses, complainants, defendants, collaborators, and client contacts must be created or improved, with unique records per RUT that eliminate duplicates and capitalization variations. When a defendant is updated, previous records must be cleansed, retaining only the most recent one. The witness and complainant database must allow background information to be queried, new records to be incorporated promptly, and updates to be made periodically — ideally weekly — for critical clients such as Walmart. A visual indicator of the witness's employment status (active, inactive, or at another store) must be incorporated, and the system must allow the type and role of each party in internal crime events with multiple individuals involved to be correctly distinguished.","gap":"Substantially improves the quality and reliability of individual data in the system, eliminating duplicates, outdated records, and capitalization variations that hinder identification. Enables summonses and documents to be generated with accurate information, facilitates the differentiation of parties in complex events, and reduces the risk of errors from incomplete or inconsistent records.","sug":"Partially resolved in Beta — test first before deepening the requirement.","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this gap for Mexico — we are fine with adding it for us, with the exception that RUT should not be considered as it is not applicable in Mexico; similarly, we would not use its Mexican equivalent, the CURP, since currently in Mexico it does not guarantee that it corresponds to the person presenting or mentioning it.","CO":"I understand that in BETA it will be possible to parameterize data entry criteria to improve data quality.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Appears to be related to the entry and consolidation of data in the Offender model, but examples are needed for a more detailed evaluation."}},"CL-022":{"tit":"Standardization of records, notes, catalogs, and case fields","actual":"There are various inconsistencies in case fields, catalogs, and records that affect information quality. Management notes in Alliance do not follow a uniform drafting format, making it difficult to review and track cases. The offense catalog available in the system does not include several types currently being processed, forcing incorrect or incomplete records. The damages and losses tab is too specific for the diversity of offenses managed, which can distort information in dashboards and spreadsheets. Flags are not sufficiently visible when opening an event, and their placement causes them to be overlooked. The Drive for CGE client cases contains duplicated categories or ones that add no value — such as the 'Last note in Alliance' category — making it difficult to review and update information.","futura":"Case records and fields must be standardized across multiple dimensions: defining uniform drafting models for management notes by type of proceeding; updating the offense catalog to include the types currently being processed; adjusting the damages and losses tab to correctly reflect the diversity of offenses; improving the visibility and placement of flags so they are immediately visible when opening an event and more functional for the user; and purging the CGE Drive categories by removing those that duplicate information or add no operational value.","gap":"Improves the quality, consistency, and usefulness of records in the system, reducing errors stemming from outdated catalogs, notes without a uniform format, or fields poorly adapted to actual operations. Strengthens data governance and allows recorded information to be more reliable for use in reporting, case tracking, and management dashboards.","sug":"Partially resolved in Beta — the activity recording functionality in processes or the configuration of background information in legal cases should be tested first to determine whether the need has been addressed.","obs":{"MX":"Same comments as in line 90 of Chile.","CO":"I understand that in BETA it will be possible to parameterize data entry criteria to improve data quality.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations unless additional examples are provided that demonstrate gaps in Beta's functionality."}},"CL-023":{"tit":"Governance over case updates, requests, and operational records","actual":"The updating of cases, RUC requests, requirements, statements, and investigation management actions is currently performed across multiple platforms — client drives, internal drives, and Alliance — with poorly defined roles and no concurrency control mechanisms. In the RUC request drive, different team members enter information in any order, which has caused records to be overwritten and event IDs to overlap. Alliance updates are distributed among several people without a clear separation of responsibilities, increasing the risk of omissions or incorrect entries. There is no chronological log of investigation management actions, and the simultaneous use of multiple platforms increases the risk of losing information with a single click. Witness requirements and statements are currently recorded in Alliance notes, without a dedicated tab or structure for them.","futura":"A controlled update model must be established with clearly defined roles that prevent overwriting, omissions, and incorrect entries. The system must incorporate a chronological log of all investigation management actions per case, a structured record of RUC requests with concurrency control, and a dedicated tab or section for witness requirements and statements that is more expedient than free-form notes. The goal is to move toward the use of a single system or secure repository that offers the flexibility of drives and the standardization of Alliance, ensuring that no valuable information is lost during migrations or due to concurrent edits.","gap":"Strengthens operational control over case and request updates, eliminating the risk of overwriting, information loss, and omissions caused by poorly defined roles and parallel platforms. The chronological log improves the traceability of investigation management and facilitates the orderly and auditable monitoring of each case's progress.","sug":"Also include versioning and data traceability capabilities.","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this gap for Mexico — we are fine with adding it for us.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations unless additional examples are provided that demonstrate gaps in Beta's functionality."}},"CL-024":{"tit":"Integration and automation of data between systems and external sources","actual":"The transfer, updating, and organization of information between systems generates a significant operational burden. Case data — RUC, RIT, defendants, status — must be entered manually in Alliance, Excel, and Drive, generating duplicate work and a risk of inconsistencies. Files in Drive are mixed and lack systematic organization. Bulk event uploads, while enabled on the platform, depend on another team's management, causing delays and forcing manual entries to meet operational timelines, increasing the workload and risk of errors.","futura":"Data integration between the various systems — Alliance, Beta, Excel, Drive, base documents such as complaints and minutes — must be automated so that case information is loaded or updated automatically without the need for manual re-entry. Drive file organization must be managed systematically, through rules, defined responsible parties, or automation/AI support that organizes files according to pre-established criteria. Additionally, teams must be granted autonomy to perform bulk event uploads independently without relying on other departments, reducing delays and the need for additional manual entries.","gap":"Eliminates duplicate data entry between systems, reduces the risk of inconsistencies and errors from manual information transfer, and improves Drive file organization. Autonomy in bulk uploads reduces dependence on other departments, decreases operational delays, and allows the team to meet required timelines without additional manual entries.","sug":"Also include eliminating these parallel management spreadsheets.","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this gap for Mexico — we are fine with adding it for us.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. It has already been established that integration with external incident reporting software is possible. Without examples, this request does not provide sufficient information to determine how to proceed."}},"CL-019":{"tit":"Consolidation and traceability of detention hearings and associated events","actual":"The recording and cross-referencing of detention hearings is managed through two separate Excel files (RM Internal Control and RM External Control), generating duplicate sources and making efficient access to and updating of information difficult. When cross-referencing events entered by the store with those recorded by the monitoring center, comparison errors arise due to differences in amount, event detail, or time, creating confusion when identifying the corresponding detention hearing on the schedule. This process is especially critical during weekend shifts, when the time available to perform the cross-reference is limited.","futura":"Detention hearing records must be consolidated into a single source that integrates both internal and external control, facilitating access, updating, and cross-referencing of information more efficiently and user-friendly. The traceability between events, hearings, amounts, times, and event details must be more precise and clear, enabling TJ and on-call attorneys — even during weekend morning shifts — to perform the cross-reference reliably and with a smaller margin of error.","gap":"Eliminates duplicate sources in detention hearing records, improves traceability between events and hearings, and significantly reduces the margin of error in cross-referencing information. Allows TJ and on-call attorneys to complete the process more quickly and reliably, especially during critical weekend hours.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Not part of the USA operational workflow."}},"CL-008":{"tit":"Automated assignment and distribution of hearings and cases","actual":"When a hearing is shared by multiple defendants, it must be entered or updated manually in each legal case individually, generating rework and a high time investment. Attorney assignment to hearings is also done manually: the spreadsheet is downloaded, migrated data is verified for correctness and completeness, and each hearing is then assigned to an attorney one by one. Case distribution among attorneys also requires manual review and coordination, involving time lost to transfers, waiting, and managing available time slots.","futura":"The ability to assign the same hearing to multiple defendants or cases simultaneously must be made available, avoiding repetitive entry. Additionally, a consolidated spreadsheet with complete hearing information — date, time, court, hearing type, event ID, and responsible attorney — must be provided so that attorneys themselves can distribute hearings more intelligently or in an automated manner, reducing manual intervention in assignment and making better use of the team's available resources.","gap":"Eliminates repetitive entry of hearings shared among multiple defendants, reducing rework and assignment errors. More intelligent distribution of hearings among attorneys optimizes the use of team resources and reduces dependence on manual coordination, improving the speed and consistency of schedule management.","sug":"This is resolved in Beta.","obs":{"MX":"This gap is not applicable to Mexico, as it does not occur here that multiple defendants corresponding to different incidents or offenses — even of the same type — are processed in the same hearing.","CO":"Left the form unanswered.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Beta already has structured operational workflows. Examples are needed to evaluate this request in greater detail."}},"CL-007":{"tit":"Centralized and advance management of scheduled hearings","actual":"Hearing scheduling is managed through spreadsheets, planning sheets, or weekly planning sessions — generally on Thursdays — which limits visibility to the following week's hearings. There is no tool that allows future hearings for each case to be consulted in advance and on a continuous basis. The hearings spreadsheet does not always correctly reflect the responsible attorney, requiring each case to be manually reviewed to identify one's own hearings. For SPPE/AJO/AJOS hearings, the general spreadsheet must be manually downloaded and filtered twice per week by flag, hearing type, and date. Additionally, the platform only allows one option to be added per scheduled hearing, preventing hearings covering multiple matters simultaneously from being characterized.","futura":"A centralized hearing module or view is needed that allows each user to consult their scheduled hearings — both their own and those that are delayed or pending update — in advance and on a continuous basis, without depending on weekly spreadsheets. It must accurately reflect the responsible attorney for each case and allow filtering by attorney, hearing type, unit, or client. For the SPPE unit, it must include an exclusive view of AJOS and AJO hearings that avoids recurring manual filtering. It must also allow multiple characterization options per scheduled hearing to be incorporated, so that each matter in the same hearing does not need to be recorded separately.","gap":"Improves the legal team's advance planning by allowing future hearings to be consulted without depending on weekly spreadsheets, reduces recurring manual filtering in units such as SPPE, and minimizes the risk of missing one's own or delayed hearings. The ability to characterize multiple matters in the same hearing eliminates duplicate records and improves information quality.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"We have a weekly report of upcoming hearings and likewise have daily access to the hearings data spreadsheet for activity planning.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Beta already has structured operational workflows. Examples are needed to evaluate this request in greater detail."}},"CL-005":{"tit":"Auto-population and data integration in case documents and requests","actual":"Data already available in the system — such as event ID, client, store, amount, report number, party type, RUT, and full name — must be entered manually into operational drives, RUC request forms, hearing instructions, and other documents associated with the case. This forces attorneys to repeatedly enter instructions already recorded on a weekly basis, search prior drives to copy instructions for rescheduled cases, and transfer information between different system tabs to external documents, generating rework, delays, and risk of error.","futura":"The goal is for event or case data to be automatically integrated and auto-populated in associated documents and requests, such as RUC requests to the Prosecutor's Office, hearing instructions, operational drives, and other linked records. This would eliminate double data entry, allow prior instructions from rescheduled cases to be reused without manual searching, and ensure information consistency between the system and generated documents, reducing attorneys' weekly operational workload.","gap":"Eliminates double entry of information already available in the system, reducing attorneys' weekly operational burden and the risk of errors from manual data transfer. Improves data consistency across platforms and allows prior instructions in rescheduled cases to be reused without manual searching or copying.","sug":"Generating briefs from Alliance could avoid this, but each workflow must be reviewed individually to find a solution.","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this gap for Mexico — we are fine with adding it for us.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Auto-populating case data increases the risk of incorrect entries. It is not clear what is being requested without examples."}},"CL-017":{"tit":"Bulk updating of flags and operational records","actual":"Flags on Alliance events must be activated manually one by one: when responding to an information request, the user must access the platform, search for each event, and activate the corresponding flag. This process adds an extra step to the management workflow, increases the workload, and makes it difficult to keep operational records consistently up to date.","futura":"A bulk flag update mechanism must be implemented in Alliance through a shared drive where answered requests are recorded, allowing the IT team to perform platform updates via periodic bulk uploads — weekly or monthly — without the need for individual activation per event.","gap":"Reduces the operational burden associated with manually activating flags event by event, decreases the total time invested in this process, and improves the consistency of records on the platform. Allows information to be kept systematically up to date, with less dependence on individual user availability.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"Functional for the legal team in Colombia — flag activation is done manually or must be submitted via a ticket while simultaneously maintaining an Excel file for corrections.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. The bulk upload process is currently mostly automated via Google Drive > Alliance."}},"CL-001":{"tit":"Integrated multimedia evidence and document Viewer","actual":"Currently, documents and images associated with evidence cannot be correctly viewed from Beta, or can only be viewed in a limited way, forcing users to download files to review them in full and making it difficult to efficiently access relevant event information.","futura":"Beta must include an integrated Viewer for documents, images, and multimedia evidence, enabling files to be reviewed in full, stably, and without needing to download them — including relevant event documents, images, evidence backups, and background information associated with case management.","gap":"Eliminates the need to download files in order to review them, speeding up access to relevant evidence and reducing the time lost on tasks that currently depend on individual downloads. Improves the user experience and enables a more agile and continuous review of case background information.","sug":"For this functionality to be complete, it may need to consider incorporating a CMS.","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this gap for Mexico — we are fine with adding it for us.","CO":"This feature will be useful when Beta is implemented at 100% in Colombia.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Attachments can be added to cases, incidents, and touchpoints within Beta. Storing this information outside of Alliance poses data security risks, and syncing the system with external repositories is discouraged."}},"CL-002":{"tit":"Centralized repository and synchronization of investigative documentation","actual":"Documentation, evidence, videos, notifications, and files associated with events or cases are currently managed across dispersed repositories — through emails, individual Drive folders, manual uploads, or direct requests to specific clients and stores. There is no centralized repository accessible to the entire team, leading to disorder, document duplication, management errors, operational delays, dependence on specific individuals, and difficulty accessing information in a timely manner. Documents are uploaded manually on a case-by-case basis within the platform, and file uploading and downloading is unstable and prone to errors.","futura":"Investigative files, documents, notifications, videos, evidence, and other files must be centralized, synchronized, and automatically integrated into the corresponding case or event on the platform. This involves having a repository accessible across the entire team, with direct integration with Google Drive folders by client, automatic document synchronization, stable file upload and download, and automatic storage of received notifications linked to the legal case. Clients would have unique Drive links to upload evidence autonomously, and any attorney could consult and download information without depending on third parties.","gap":"Centralizes case documentation in a single source accessible to the entire team, eliminating dependence on emails, individual drives, and manual requests. Reduces document duplication, improves evidence traceability, and allows any attorney to access information autonomously and in a timely manner, without depending on specific individuals.","sug":"For this functionality to be complete, it may need to consider incorporating a CMS.","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this gap for Mexico — we are fine with adding it for us.","CO":"This proposal aligns with the centralized management of videos, photos, and documents. Having information organized in a single location in BETA will enable more efficient access for the entire team, avoiding dependence on third parties or individuals who are no longer on shift.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Attachments can be added to cases, incidents, and touchpoints within Beta. Storing this information outside of Alliance poses data security risks, and syncing the system with external repositories is discouraged."}},"CL-003":{"tit":"Standardization and automatic organization of investigative documentation","actual":"Documentation received from the Prosecutor's Office or other external sources arrives in a disorganized state, without clear naming conventions or uniform classification criteria. No standardized procedure exists for its reception and organization, so each attorney must manually review file by file to identify its content. This involves a high time investment and carries the risk of overlooking information relevant to the case.","futura":"An internal document reception and organization protocol is sought that includes minimum classification criteria, standardized naming conventions, and a folder structure for documentation from third parties. Ideally, this protocol would be supported by automation tools, artificial intelligence, or administrative support that allows information to be sorted and categorized before legal review, reducing the time spent on organizational tasks and minimizing the risk of omissions.","gap":"Reduces the time invested in documentary organization tasks prior to legal review, lowers the risk of overlooking relevant background information, and improves the quality and consistency of records. Allows attorneys to dedicate their time to substantive analysis rather than manual file classification.","sug":"This involves designing a document reception workflow that enables better organization and analysis of received documents. It potentially requires only a people process supported by an appropriate technology tool (CMS).","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this gap for Mexico — we are fine with adding it for us.","CO":"Having an AI assistant that identifies summonses from the Prosecutor's Office or courts and that, through automation, schedules the activities in BETA, will ensure that all information is properly recorded. In this way, the team will be able to optimize their time and focus on other higher-value activities, and all judicial proceedings will be attended to in a timely manner.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Attachments can be added to cases, incidents, and touchpoints within Beta. Storing this information outside of Alliance poses data security risks, and syncing the system with external repositories is discouraged."}},"CL-006":{"tit":"Unified intelligent search engine for events and documents","actual":"Searching for events, cases, individuals, documents, and related events is currently slow, unintuitive, and dependent on multiple prior steps — such as selecting modules, creating views, defining mandatory date ranges, or opening separate windows. The search engine is not embedded directly in the main interface and does not support flexible queries by defendant name, RUT, RIT, RUC, or event ID without additional configuration. This makes it difficult to locate information efficiently and slows down the workflow.","futura":"An intelligent, unified search engine must be implemented and embedded directly in the platform's main interface, enabling events, documents, individuals, defendants, RUT, RUC, RIT, and event IDs to be found quickly and without unnecessary prior steps. The search engine must offer intuitive — not literal — filters, must not require a mandatory date range or allow fixed predefined ranges, and must consolidate in a single entry the search of events, individuals, and legal matters, as was available in the Legacy version, but with expanded capabilities to identify related events.","gap":"Speeds up access to key case information, reducing the time spent on searches and eliminating unnecessary steps. Improves user experience and team operational efficiency, enabling events, individuals, and documents to be located in less time and with greater precision.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"Once BETA is operational in Colombia, this search engine will be useful.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Examples are needed to evaluate this request in greater detail."}},"CL-012":{"tit":"Optimized operational search engine for legal events","actual":"Searching for legal events in Beta requires entering a date range as a mandatory prior step before searching for a specific event or ID, which slows down the process and adds unnecessary steps for those who need to quickly access a specific case.","futura":"Legal event searches must be able to be performed directly by ID or other specific criteria, without requiring a prior date range to be defined. This would allow events to be accessed more quickly and directly, reducing the steps needed to locate a specific case in daily operations.","gap":"Speeds up access to specific events by eliminating mandatory steps that add no value to a targeted search, improving daily operational efficiency and reducing friction in platform use for those who need to locate a case immediately.","sug":"The Viewer is for investigating and analyzing the data it presents; adjusting the date is not necessary since a range can be predefined and reused. The required functionality is a search that allows an immediate action to be taken.","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this gap for Mexico — we are fine with adding it for us.","CO":"This functionality will be useful once access to BETA is available, as it will allow events or legal cases to be searched more smoothly.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Beta already has search functionality. Examples are needed to evaluate this request in greater detail."}},"CL-021":{"tit":"Universal search engine and search filter optimization","actual":"Searching for events, cases, and individuals in Alliance/Beta is currently slow, impractical, and fragmented. In Beta, multiple prior steps must be followed before searching for a data point, and the search engine requires selecting different categories depending on whether the search is by ID, defendant name, related party, or another parameter, without consolidating results in a single view. In Legacy the search is more direct and visible, but in Beta this experience has been lost. The available filters do not work with the intuitiveness of an Excel spreadsheet, and the system does not tolerate blank spaces or spelling variations, which slows searches and affects operational efficiency.","futura":"A universal, fast search engine integrated into Beta's main interface is needed — without opening a separate window — that allows events, cases, and individuals to be found with a single search field, whether by ID, defendant name, RUT, RUC, related party, or other parameters. The search engine must be intelligent, tolerating blank spaces and spelling variations. Filters must operate with logic more similar to that of an Excel spreadsheet, facilitating segmentation and direct access to relevant information more quickly and smoothly.","gap":"Reduces the time spent on fragmented searches and improves the user experience by consolidating the search for events, cases, and individuals into a single field. Tolerance for spelling variations and more intuitive filter logic reduce operational friction and allow the team to access relevant information with greater speed and precision.","sug":"Search engine integrated into the module.","obs":{"MX":"We believe this gap is repeated even in those previously described for Chile and likewise for Mexico, which qualifies it as cross-cutting.","CO":"May be useful once BETA is activated in Colombia.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Search functionalities can always be improved, but they still require users to define what they want to search for. Examples are needed for a more detailed evaluation."}},"CL-026":{"tit":"Performance, stability, and usability improvements for Alliance/Beta","actual":"Alliance/Beta experiences recurring slowness and freezing that affect daily operations. When entering an ID to search for case information, the system responds extremely slowly or hangs, forcing users to refresh or restart the session. This occurs especially when querying information by tabs, updating tags, or creating events. Slow response times directly impact the ability of lawyers and legal technicians to respond promptly to client requests, which in many cases are time-sensitive.","futura":"Alliance/Beta must improve in performance, stability, and response speed so that querying, updating, and recording information is faster, smoother, and more reliable. The system must operate with greater agility, reduce freezing, prevent session drops, and ensure stable response times when querying, updating, or recording information.","gap":"Improves operational continuity by reducing wait times, freezing, and session restarts that interrupt workflow. Enables lawyers and legal technicians to respond more promptly to client requests, improving the platform user experience and reducing operational frustration associated with system instability.","sug":"This is initially resolved by migrating to Beta","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Site availability commitments are managed through IT and have previously been defined based on external cybersecurity audits."}},"CL-027":{"tit":"Logging and tracking of private defense case management activities","actual":"There is currently no specific module or functionality for recording and tracking the proceedings, hearings, and procedural steps associated with private defense cases involving internal criminal activity. This type of case has distinctive characteristics that are not adequately covered by the general workflows available in the system.","futura":"A specific module is required within the platform to record, control, and monitor the proceedings, hearings, and procedural steps carried out in private defense cases related to internal criminal activity, with the structure and traceability needed to manage this type of case in a differentiated manner.","gap":"Addresses a significant functional gap by incorporating traceability and control over a category of cases that currently lacks structured support in the system. It allows private defense cases involving internal criminal activity to be managed with the same rigor as the rest of the portfolio, reducing the risk of omissions and improving the tracking of proceedings and hearings.","sug":"To be resolved in Beta","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this for Mexico — we are fine with adopting it for us.","CO":"This feature will be functional once we have access to BETA.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations."}},"CL-028":{"tit":"Automated legal classification through UTM value integration","actual":"The legal classification of petty theft or misdemeanor theft depends on the amount stolen and the current UTM value, which changes daily. However, the amount recorded in Alliance does not accurately reflect the UTM value on the date the incident occurred, making it impossible to determine with precision whether the offense qualifies as petty theft (Art. 446 Nos. 1, 2, or 3) or as a misdemeanor theft.","futura":"Alliance/Beta must automatically integrate the current UTM value at the time events or legal cases are created, so the system can calculate and assist in determining the legal classification of the offense based on the amount stolen and applicable regulations, correctly distinguishing between petty theft and misdemeanor theft without depending on the user's manual judgment.","gap":"Reduces the risk of errors in the legal classification of offenses by automatically incorporating the UTM value in effect at the time of the incident, improving the accuracy and consistency of the record. Decreases dependence on the user's manual judgment for a determination that has direct implications for the legal strategy and for the classification of the criminal offense.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We consider this gap does not apply to Mexico and that it even conflicts with the classification that would be given under the 3-tier legal strategy.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. How are UTM parameters currently being recorded manually? It is unclear whether our URLs use UTM tracking at this stage."}},"CL-029":{"tit":"Flexible management of tasks, hearings, and case procedural history","actual":"In Legacy it was possible to review the full history of a case with a single click, including completed tasks and notes added by users. Tasks could also be deleted when duplicated or scheduled by error, and the linear hearing workflow prevented skipping mandatory steps. In Beta, while scheduling hearings is faster, tasks appear as independent items without integrated historical traceability, they cannot be deleted — only their date or assigned user can be modified — and the absence of a mandatory linear workflow creates a risk of omitting relevant information, such as witness data, when recording proceedings.","futura":"Beta must allow more flexible and traceable management of tasks, hearings, and case history, including the ability to review the full case history with integrated tasks and notes, correct or delete erroneous or duplicate tasks, and preserve relevant witness information linked to the hearing workflow. Without imposing a rigid workflow that slows operations, the system must prevent critical procedural elements from being omitted when scheduling new proceedings.","gap":"Restores the case historical traceability lost during the migration to Beta, allowing users to review the full status of proceedings and notes without leaving the workflow. The ability to correct erroneous tasks and preserve witness information reduces the risk of critical procedural omissions and improves the quality of case records throughout the lifecycle of each matter.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"This feature will be functional once we have access to BETA.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations unless additional examples are provided that demonstrate gaps in Beta functionality."}},"CL-030":{"tit":"Automatic integration with the Judiciary for procedural status updates","actual":"Updating procedural information for cases depends on manual entry or review of background records, with no direct connection to information published by the Judiciary. As a result, procedural developments in a case within the judicial system are not automatically reflected in the platform.","futura":"Beta must be linked to information published by the Judiciary so that, when a legal case is created or identified using RUT, RIT, and court, the system can automatically generate or update the corresponding procedural tasks in the matter based on the background records available in the judicial registry.","gap":"Reduces the burden of manually updating procedural background records, improves the timeliness with which judicial case developments are reflected in the platform, and lowers the risk of overlooking relevant procedural steps. Strengthens the continuity of case management by keeping the system aligned with the actual status of matters in the Judiciary.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We consider this does not apply to Mexico, since the judicial system is not uniform across the national territory and does not have the same tools and infrastructure.","CO":"This functionality would be especially useful in Colombia, as it would allow integration and linkage with public sources for querying and validating background records, facilitating information verification.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations unless additional examples are provided that demonstrate gaps in Beta functionality."}},"CL-031":{"tit":"AI assistance for background analysis and complaint drafting","actual":"The drafting of complaints is slowed when clients submit lengthy reports containing large volumes of information. The attorney must manually read, analyze, and extract the relevant background records before being able to prepare the submission, resulting in a significant loss of time during the pre-drafting stage.","futura":"AI support must be incorporated to analyze the lengthy reports submitted by clients, identify and extract the relevant background records for the complaint, and assist the attorney in drafting the document, reducing review and preparation times without replacing the validation and legal judgment of the attorney in charge.","gap":"Reduces the time spent manually reading and extracting background records from lengthy reports, accelerating the complaint preparation process without replacing the attorney's legal judgment. Improves responsiveness in cases with high document volume and allows the legal team to focus on validation and argumentation rather than reading and summarizing tasks.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this for Mexico — we are fine with adopting it for us.","CO":"This is identified as a high-value opportunity that reduces working time spent reading lengthy reports and building the statement of facts. AI is a support tool but will not replace the judgment and responsibility of the attorney in charge, who ultimately signs each complaint.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations unless additional examples are provided that demonstrate gaps in Beta functionality."}},"CL-032":{"tit":"Unified record of procedural outcomes, sentences, and conditions","actual":"When recording the outcome of a conviction or a conditional suspension of proceedings (SCP), the system requires completing a separate form or workflow for each element: in the case of convictions, the workflow must be repeated for each sentence — fine, imprisonment, form of compliance; in the case of SCP, a new outcome must be entered for each agreed condition. This generates repetitive steps, greater operational burden, and a risk of errors or omissions in the record.","futura":"Procedural outcomes must be recordable in a unified manner within a single form: for convictions, it must be possible to enter all sentences for the convicted person simultaneously — fine, custodial sentence, and form of compliance — without repeating the workflow for each one; for SCP, each condition must be addable via a button that enables an additional field within the same outcome record, avoiding the need to start a new entry for each condition.","gap":"Reduces the operational burden and risk of error when recording complex procedural outcomes by eliminating the repetition of workflows for each sentence or condition. Improves the completeness and consistency of outcome records, facilitates subsequent review of convictions and SCP, and reduces the time spent on case-closing actions.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"Functional for the legal team in Colombia once BETA is implemented.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations unless additional examples are provided that demonstrate gaps in Beta functionality."}},"CL-033":{"tit":"Editing and standardization of procedural data and legal workflows in Beta","actual":"Two needs exist for adjustment and continuity of procedural case information. On one hand, modifying case identification data — RIT, RUC, and court — is currently cumbersome in Alliance. On the other hand, legal workflows with their stages and procedural statuses need to be updated or migrated to Beta while preserving relevant information, with no loss of continuity in the management of each matter.","futura":"Controlled editing of case identification data — RIT, RUC, and court — must be made simpler and more straightforward. Beta must also incorporate standardized legal workflows that faithfully carry over the legal stages, procedural status, and management continuity currently in place, ensuring that each matter retains its relevant information when migrated or updated in the new platform.","gap":"Facilitates the timely correction of case identification data, preventing errors in RIT, RUC, or court from persisting in the system due to the lack of an agile editing mechanism. The standardization of legal workflows in Beta ensures continuity in case management during migration, reducing the risk of losing relevant procedural information.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations unless additional examples are provided that demonstrate gaps in Beta functionality."}},"CL-034":{"tit":"Automated alerts and reporting for events, alarms, and priority gangs","actual":"The review of alarms, events, prosecutable cases, and potential priority gangs is currently performed entirely manually. Users build their own filters in Gmail to manage received alarms, and identifying priority gangs requires reviewing cases one by one to determine whether the defined criteria for flagging them with the corresponding priority level are met. The assessment of variables such as event type, recidivism, gang involvement, known suspects, or criminal patterns depends entirely on the user's judgment and availability, generating high time consumption and a risk that relevant events will not be prioritized in a timely manner.","futura":"An automated alert and reporting system must be implemented to filter, prioritize, and notify relevant events according to predefined criteria, such as event type, priority gangs, recidivism, known suspects, or criminal patterns. The system must generate daily reports with alarms filtered by unit or criterion, send email alerts when a gang meets the established requirements, and perform automatic flagging of priority gangs, reducing reliance on manual review and improving the speed of response to priority cases.","gap":"Substantially improves the ability to prioritize relevant cases by automating the detection of priority gangs, recidivists, and known suspects, reducing the risk that critical events will not be identified in a timely manner. Frees up team time for substantive analysis by replacing manual filters with a systematic alert and periodic reporting system.","sug":"Add that management systems external to Alliance be eliminated","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this for Mexico — we are fine with adopting it for us.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations unless additional examples are provided that demonstrate gaps in Beta functionality."}},"CL-035":{"tit":"Automatic event classification by unit and operational criteria","actual":"Incoming events must be manually reviewed and classified by the team, assigning the corresponding unit according to predefined criteria. This process involves logging into Alliance, reviewing each event one by one, and manually tagging the assigned unit, generating high operational time consumption and dependence on user availability to keep records up to date.","futura":"An automation must be implemented to classify events automatically at the time they are entered into the system, applying the predefined criteria to directly assign the corresponding unit. In this way, each event would be recorded in Alliance with the correct tag from the outset, significantly reducing manual intervention and processing times.","gap":"Reduces the operational time dedicated to manual event classification, ensuring that each case is correctly assigned from the moment it enters the system. Decreases dependence on user availability and the risk of late or incorrect classifications that could affect subsequent case management.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"This gap differs in wording from Mexico's version; however, it aligns in objective with the one linked to 3-tier legal strategy classification.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Limited applicability within the current USA operating model."}},"CL-036":{"tit":"Advanced video, image, and CCTV analysis for pattern detection","actual":"The analysis of videos, images, and CCTV records is currently performed with basic tools or entirely manually, making it difficult to improve image quality — zoom, sharpness, lighting — identify recurring subjects, detect hotspots, generate useful frames, and establish links between events or gangs. This limitation leaves the team at a disadvantage compared to other stakeholders such as Police and the Public Prosecutor's Office, which already use specialized digital tools for these tasks. It should be expressly noted that no analysis can be performed entirely through generative AI, given the gaps and hallucinations extensively documented by academia since 2023.","futura":"Specialized software and technological tools for video, image, and CCTV analysis are required, capable of improving image quality with filters, lossless zoom, and lighting adjustment; detecting hotspots in video using technology not necessarily based on generative AI; identifying visual patterns and recurring subjects; generating frames; and supporting the linking of events, persons, or gangs. These tools must operate as technical support for human analysis, complementing investigative judgment without replacing it.","gap":"Strengthens the team's investigative capacity by providing specialized tools for CCTV analysis, improving image quality and the detection of visual patterns that currently escape manual analysis. Reduces the disadvantage relative to other stakeholders and increases effectiveness in identifying subjects, linking events, and detecting hotspots, always as a complement to the analyst's judgment.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this for Mexico — we are fine with adopting it for us.","CO":"This strengthens the video analyst's work and optimizes their time, since they currently have to dedicate several hours to viewing and analyzing audiovisual content.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations at this stage. It is partially covered by the Offender model linking, but full AI-based analysis of all multimedia content entered in incidents and cases requires significant review from a legal and resource perspective."}},"CL-037":{"tit":"Advanced identity integration and external sources for investigation","actual":"The investigation of individuals involved in criminal activity relies almost exclusively on open-source analysis, which proves insufficient when subjects avoid leaving a digital or civil registry trail — no passport, national ID, or fingerprint record. This practice, documented in Prosecutor's Office studies as a deliberate pattern to evade detection, limits investigative effectiveness and reduces the ability to support judicial measures when sufficient evidence is lacking.","futura":"External services must be sought, evaluated, and potentially contracted to allow persons to be cross-referenced and identified using sources beyond open ones, strengthening the team's investigative capacity. Additionally, exploring the creation of public-private alliances — such as technical working groups or other forums — is proposed to facilitate the identification of subjects and improve inter-institutional collaboration in crime prevention and investigation.","gap":"Strengthens investigative capacity through the integration of authorized external sources, institutional agreements, or mechanisms permitted under applicable regulations, allowing available information to be supplemented, improving the identification of persons or relevant links, and reducing dependence on fragmented manual searches. This improves the quality of investigative analysis, increases responsiveness, and allows complex cases to be supported with greater solidity.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this for Mexico — we are fine with adopting it for us. The only clarification is that in Mexico we would do this through the Institutional Relations department, without the need for external providers.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations without specific examples."}},"CL-038":{"tit":"Integration of investigative information for technical reports and linkages","actual":"The preparation of technical reports and the identification of investigative linkages requires integrating information from multiple sources: images, background records, video analysis, external sources, and system records. There is currently no consolidated tool that organizes, connects, or facilitates collaborative work with these inputs, making the process slower, more fragmented, and more dependent on the individual analyst's judgment.","futura":"A tool or functionality is required that integrates the various investigative inputs — visual background records, external sources, system records, and identity information — to facilitate the preparation of technical reports, the identification of linkages between persons or events, and support for preventive criminal analysis. This integration must operate as support for the analyst, without replacing their judgment or presenting automated results as definitive conclusions.","gap":"Reduces the fragmentation of the technical report preparation process by integrating the various investigative inputs into a single tool, improving the efficiency and quality of analysis. Facilitates the identification of linkages between persons and events, and strengthens technical support for decision-making in the area of crime prevention and investigation.","sug":"Add to the CMS concept the inclusion of comment management, tags, and other elements that support the investigation","obs":{"MX":"We consider this would not be operational for Mexico, given potential conflicts with legislation in this area.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations at this stage. It is partially covered by the Offender model linking."}},"CL-039":{"tit":"Automated creation and registration of legal cases from events","actual":"The creation of complaints, criminal complaints, and legal cases requires manually entering information into the system, even when much of that data is already available in the event or in the platform. This includes suspect identification data, location, address, designated attorney, and complaint filing status. The process is entirely manual, generating duplicate work, delays, risk of error, and dependence on the user to complete data that could be captured automatically from existing information.","futura":"The creation and registration of legal cases from Beta must be automated, allowing information available in the event to be transferred automatically to the corresponding legal case or complaint, including suspect data, location, address, responsible attorney, and complaint status. The functionality must create the case immediately — so that the complaint and system entry occur in parallel — with automatic assignment of the responsible attorney where applicable, eliminating duplicate data entry and reducing the operational burden.","gap":"Eliminates duplicate data entry between the event and the legal case, reducing case creation time, the risk of errors from manual data transfer, and user dependence. Allows the complaint and the system record to be created in parallel, accelerating the start of processing and improving traceability from the very first moment of the case.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations unless additional examples are provided that demonstrate gaps in Beta functionality."}},"CL-040":{"tit":"Unified suspect search and creation","actual":"In the previous workflow it was possible to determine in a single step whether a suspect already existed in the system or needed to be created: upon entering a name or RUT, the system would directly indicate whether there were matches or not. In Beta, by contrast, the user must first search the database and then, if the suspect is not found, perform a separate step to create them, fragmenting the workflow and adding unnecessary steps.","futura":"Beta must allow suspects to be searched and created within the same functional workflow, so that upon entering a name or RUT the system identifies existing matches and, if no prior records are found, immediately enables the creation of the suspect without forcing the user to leave the workflow or repeat additional steps.","gap":"Simplifies and unifies the suspect entry workflow, reducing the number of steps required and improving the user experience in a recurring operation. Decreases the risk of creating duplicate records due to incomplete searches and accelerates the process of linking suspects to new cases or events.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations unless additional examples are provided that demonstrate gaps in Beta functionality and in the future Offender model functionalities previously proposed."}},"CL-041":{"tit":"Automated SIAU movement queries","actual":"Reviewing movements in SIAU is currently performed manually, entering each case individually to check its status or progress. This process entails a significant operational burden and dependence on individual queries, with no integration that would allow consolidated or automated access to the information.","futura":"SIAU movement queries must be automated or integrated into the platform so the system can identify, update, or display relevant movements for each case without requiring manual review case by case, reducing the operational burden and enabling more efficient tracking of case statuses.","gap":"Reduces the operational burden associated with manually reviewing SIAU case by case, improving the efficiency of procedural tracking and allowing the team to identify relevant movements more quickly. Decreases the risk of overlooking important procedural steps due to a lack of timely queries.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We consider this would not be applicable to Mexico.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations unless additional examples are provided."}},"CL-042":{"tit":"Expanded quick-view of case information","actual":"Case search results display limited information: date, time, ID, client, store, and case status. To access relevant background records — such as whether a complaint has been filed or suspect data — the user must open each record individually, slowing down the review and making it difficult to quickly assess the status of multiple cases.","futura":"The quick-view of search results must be expanded to include key case data directly in the list, such as complaint filing status, suspect name and RUT, and other relevant background records. This would allow users to quickly assess the content and status of each case without needing to open each record individually.","gap":"Improves efficiency when reviewing multiple cases by allowing relevant background records to be assessed directly from the search results list, without needing to open each record individually. Reduces navigation time and facilitates the prioritization and tracking of the case portfolio status.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations unless additional examples are provided that demonstrate gaps in Beta functionality."}},"CL-043":{"tit":"Infrastructure and connectivity for CCTV event review","actual":"The review of CCTV events and video extraction depends on technical conditions that are not always adequate. At clients such as Walmart, internet connectivity problems are constant — with signal losses that interrupt the review — and no offline alternative exists to continue working. The CCTV team shares a single computer between two people, preventing both from advancing simultaneously in their tasks. Additionally, the available equipment — computers and mobile phones — does not always have the performance, processing capacity, or screen quality required for optimal image and video analysis.","futura":"The technical infrastructure for CCTV review and video analysis must be strengthened. This includes improving connection stability — for example, through wired connections where applicable — enabling the ability to download or review events without an internet connection, installing additional workstations so that more than one user can operate simultaneously in the same space, and providing adequate equipment with higher screen resolution and better processing capacity. The goal is to enable faster, continuous, and more efficient review of events and incidents, without depending on the availability of a single device or an unstable connection.","gap":"Improves the continuity and quality of CCTV analysis by eliminating dependence on unstable connections and shared equipment that interrupts workflow. Allows more than one user to progress simultaneously, increases processing capacity for image and video analysis, and reduces event and incident review times for clients such as Walmart.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations unless additional examples are provided."}},"CL-044":{"tit":"Corporate mobile equipment upgrade","actual":"Corporate phones assigned for work use exhibit poor performance, slowness, and operational failures that make them inefficient for daily tasks. In practice, users end up resorting to their personal devices to carry out their operational tasks, since the equipment provided by the company is too slow to be used effectively.","futura":"Corporate mobile equipment must be improved or replaced, providing devices with sufficient performance, greater response speed, and operational stability. The phones provided must allow work tasks to be completed effectively, eliminating the need to use personal devices and preventing equipment slowness from affecting the timing and quality of case management.","gap":"Eliminates dependence on personal devices for work-related tasks, improving information security and ensuring that the team can operate with functional corporate tools. Reduces time lost due to slow equipment and improves the user experience and responsiveness of the field team.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"It would be important to review this aspect, especially in Colombia, where some mobile devices have limitations resulting from use and wear, which can affect their optimal functioning. This becomes more relevant if the team is expected to update information in real time through the application, so it would be advisable to assess device compatibility, performance, and minimum requirements.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations unless additional examples are provided."}},"CL-045":{"tit":"Improved IT support response times","actual":"Response times for IT support tickets are slow relative to the urgency that the legal team's requests typically carry. Since many of these requests directly affect the progress or status of cases, delays in handling them can impact operational continuity and legal deadlines.","futura":"The IT ticket response process must be streamlined by incorporating prioritization criteria based on the operational or legal impact of each request. Tickets affecting active cases, event review, or the team's operational continuity must receive faster and more timely attention, reducing wait times in urgent situations.","gap":"Reduces the impact of technical problems on the legal team's operational continuity by prioritizing ticket handling according to its relevance to active cases or critical deadlines. Improves responsiveness to IT incidents that today can delay legal management and affect compliance with procedural deadlines.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this for Mexico — we are fine with adopting it for us.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Greater visibility into IT support response times and SLAs is always welcome."}},"CO-001":{"tit":"Data export with custom filters","actual":"Export of legal information with preset filters, disaggregated or limited, making it difficult to generate reports tailored to specific client needs.","futura":"Export of information with custom filters, no time limits, and the ability to consolidate by account or corporate group.","gap":"Streamlines report generation, improves analysis, and enhances presentation of results.","sug":"Create new Viewer views to address this need","obs":{"MX":"We believe this gap has the same objective as the gaps noted in lines 2 and 23 of Mexico — though not identical, its solution approach is through filters; that said, this further supports it being a cross-cutting gap.","CO":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. This looks more like a Discovery solution than a Viewer solution."}},"CO-002":{"tit":"Non-linear legal workflow management","actual":"Rigid, linear legal workflow with repetitive validations and mandatory steps that do not reflect procedural reality and do not allow for reversals or proper case closures.","futura":"Flexible, non-linear legal workflow adapted to legal reality, allowing reversals, early closures, and consistent recording of outcomes without unnecessary steps.","gap":"Improves traceability, reduces rework, and optimizes operational timelines.","sug":"Use the new legal case management tool","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Beta is not rigid and already allows reversals and proper closures."}},"CO-003":{"tit":"Unified management of multiple proceedings","actual":"Tasks, hearings, and workflows are handled individually per offender, even when they belong to the same proceeding, generating duplication and operational burden.","futura":"Unified or bulk management of tasks, hearings, and workflows for multiple offenders within the same legal proceeding.","gap":"Reduces time, avoids rework, and improves information control.","sug":"Use the new legal case management tool","obs":{"MX":"We believe this gap would not be applicable to Mexico and that, if enabled, it would lead to poor data management (incorrect information), given that in Mexico two or more individuals involved in a legal case may have different legal statuses or even be at different stages of the process at the time of completion.","CO":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Beta supports both single-suspect and multi-suspect cases."}},"CO-004":{"tit":"Automation of legal information updates and integration","actual":"Manual processes for updating prosecutor offices, recidivism records, hearings, appraisals, and briefs, resulting in delays and error risk.","futura":"Automation of updates, recidivism detection, brief generation, and synchronization with external sources.","gap":"Optimizes time, improves data quality, and reduces operational errors.","sug":"New functionalities must be implemented in addition to using the new legal management tool","obs":{"MX":"We consider this partially functional for us: regarding automation of updates, we would be fine with including it for Mexico.","CO":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. Email updates are already sent from Alliance. Syncing with external sources involves enormous complexity that must be taken into account."}},"CO-005":{"tit":"Standardization of catalogs and data structures","actual":"Unrestricted creation of products, modus operandi, offenses, and records with errors, duplicates, or open categories that affect information quality.","futura":"Definition of catalogs, closed lists, or standardized structures for products, offenses, modus operandi, and key records.","gap":"Improves data quality, analysis, and consistency in reports.","sug":"Use the new legal case management tool","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this for Mexico; we are fine with including it for us.","CO":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Data governance is already covered within the Offender model, but the system already records updates to case files, incidents, and touchpoints. Insights manages data completeness and Operations manages data quality."}},"CO-006":{"tit":"Bulk upload and centralization of evidence","actual":"Restrictions on file uploads (size, type, quantity) and the need to upload documents one by one or keep them in external sources.","futura":"Bulk upload, support for multiple formats (including video and Excel), and centralization of evidence within the system.","gap":"Optimizes time, improves access, and centralizes information.","sug":"Modify the current file management functionality","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this for Mexico; we are fine with including it for us.","CO":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. It is not part of the USA operational workflow."}},"CO-007":{"tit":"Automatic resource assignment","actual":"Manual assignment of attorneys, prosecutor offices, or responsible parties, with risk of errors, inconsistencies, or incorrect assignments.","futura":"Automatic assignment based on rules, scheduling, or integration with external sources.","gap":"Improves efficiency, prevents errors, and ensures correct assignment.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We believe this approach does not apply to Mexico, given that one of our own gaps seeks assignment through Beta according to the determination of the operating coordinator of resources.","CO":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CL":"The solution is interesting · Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. It is not part of the USA operational workflow."}},"CO-008":{"tit":"Automated task and alert management","actual":"Events or tasks go untracked, remain in draft, or contain incomplete information, without proper alerts or control.","futura":"Implementation of alerts, automatic follow-up, and control of pending or incomplete tasks.","gap":"Improves operational control and process follow-up.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We conclude that this gap coincides with the one described in line 52 of Mexico — different in wording but with the same approach and objective.","CO":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CL":"This would be useful for follow-up on, for example, witness statements, information pending from the client, and tasks requiring repeated email reminders · Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. It is not part of the USA operational workflow."}},"CO-009":{"tit":"Process optimization through elimination of redundancies","actual":"Duplicate questions, records, tasks, or processes that generate rework and time loss in operations.","futura":"Elimination of redundancies and simplification of processes through single or automated validations.","gap":"Reduces rework and optimizes time.","sug":"It is suggested to develop functionality to enable this type of management","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. It is not part of the USA operational workflow."}},"CO-010":{"tit":"Automatic generation of reports and documents","actual":"Manual preparation of bulletins, reports, appraisals, and legal documents, consuming significant time.","futura":"Automatic generation of reports, bulletins, and documents from system information using templates.","gap":"Optimizes time, standardizes information, and reduces errors.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We conclude that this gap coincides with the one described in line 44 of Mexico — different in wording but with the same approach and objective.","CO":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. This is already automated through Discovery."}},"CO-011":{"tit":"Consolidation of offender information","actual":"Offender information spread across multiple views or incomplete, making it difficult to consult and analyze.","futura":"Consolidation of offender information into a single, structured, and complete view.","gap":"Optimizes consultation time and improves recurrence analysis.","sug":"Create a Viewer to address this need","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this for Mexico; we are fine with including it for us.","CO":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — The Offender model covers this request."}},"CO-012":{"tit":"Full traceability of actions and records","actual":"Records without user identification or with loss of relevant information within the process.","futura":"Incorporation of full traceability for actions, records, and modifications within the system.","gap":"Improves control, follow-up, and auditing of information.","sug":"Alert via an Insight or other notification","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Client incident data comes from the client. Internal data quality is managed by Operations. Insights already exist to address these gaps."}},"CO-013":{"tit":"Efficient management of mandatory fields and validations","actual":"Lack of control over the completion of key fields, or the presence of validations that block processes without adding value.","futura":"Definition of useful mandatory fields and removal of unnecessary validations.","gap":"Improves data quality and system usability.","sug":"Alert via an Insight or other notification","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CL":"Convergence: No","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Client incident data comes from the client. Internal data quality is managed by Operations. Insights already exist to address these gaps."}},"CO-014":{"tit":"Standardization of product records","actual":"Inconsistent recording of stolen products that hinders statistical analysis and information control.","futura":"Standardization of product records through structures defined by client or category.","gap":"Improves statistical analysis and information control.","sug":"Modify the product management functionality","obs":{"MX":"No comments.","CO":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CL":"Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Client incident data comes from the client. Internal data quality is managed by Operations. Insights already exist to address these gaps."}},"CO-015":{"tit":"Automatic integration with external sources","actual":"Dependence on manual queries to external systems such as SPOA for information updates.","futura":"Automatic integration with external sources for real-time data updates.","gap":"Optimizes time and improves information accuracy.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We believe this gap conflicts with the Mexico gap, in terms of the objective of entering data directly in Beta to avoid rework.","CO":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","CL":"Example: integration with the Judicial Branch website · Convergence: Yes","USA":"Not relevant to USA operations. — Not relevant to USA operations. It has already been established that integration with external incident-reporting software is possible. Without specific examples, this request does not provide enough information to determine how to proceed."}},"USA-001":{"tit":"Event accountability and ownership tracking","actual":"Comprehensive offender management and relationship mapping","futura":"Implement an integrated system that allows assigning responsibility, tracking review status, and flagging critical events directly within the platform.","gap":"Accountability: eliminates uncertainty by clearly identifying who is managing each event. Centralization: reduces reliance on external messaging tools for critical alerts. Auditability: provides a clear record of the event lifecycle from creation to review. Eliminates invisible or parallel work. Reinforces a single source of truth.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We believe this does not apply to Mexico, given the management model through client account managers.","CO":"It is important to have management Insights and traffic-light tools to enable timely and strategic follow-up on priority cases.","CL":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country.","USA":"Revisar con Jeremiah. — Se recomienda reevaluar la antigua solución de Incident Inbox."}},"USA-002":{"tit":"Event follow-up pipeline","actual":"The system operates in a binary fashion: \"Create case\" or \"No action.\" Any event requiring subsequent follow-up is managed through personal lists outside Alliance, resulting in a loss of visibility for the rest of the team.","futura":"Create a centralized \"Follow-up\" status or queue within the platform to manage events requiring future actions without the need to immediately create a legal case.","gap":"Operational visibility: gives teams and leadership a complete view of the pending workload that is currently invisible. Data preservation: ensures that historical actions and notes remain within the platform rather than in private spreadsheets. Continuity: prevents tasks from being lost when a team member is unavailable. Eliminates invisible or parallel work. Reinforces a single source of truth.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We believe this does not apply to Mexico, as there is already a section for non-legal proceedings.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Left the field blank","USA":"Revisar con Jeremiah. — Se recomienda reevaluar la antigua solución de Incident Inbox."}},"USA-003":{"tit":"Scheduled proactive case reviews","actual":"Case reviews are primarily reactive, triggered by external events, or managed through personal reminders outside the system. There is no internal mechanism to trigger a proactive review of an active case.","futura":"Incorporate an internal mechanism to schedule and track proactive reviews, ensuring that cases are monitored according to internal standards and not only by external triggers.","gap":"Risk mitigation: prevents cases from stalling, reducing legal and operational risks. Standardization: creates a consistent review cadence across the legal team. Efficiency: replaces external manual reminders with an automated workflow within the platform. Eliminates invisible or parallel work. Reinforces a single source of truth.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this for Mexico; we are fine with including it for us.","CO":"No comments.","CL":"Left the field blank","USA":"Not applicable — proposal initiated by this country."}},"USA-004":{"tit":"Comprehensive offender management and relationship mapping","actual":"The current offender management process lacks native platform support. Teams rely on insufficient manual workarounds, resulting in high operational effort, limited search capabilities, and loss of critical links between events, legal cases, and offenders.","futura":"Develop a dedicated module to manage offender profiles that automatically centralizes information and enables mapping of relationships between individuals, specific events, and legal cases.","gap":"Data integrity: restores and maintains the connection between offenders and their history within the platform, preventing information silos. Improved search capability: enables advanced filters and pattern recognition — for example, identifying repeat offenders across different cases, clients, and markets. Process automation: reduces manual burden through a structured, native environment designed for this workflow. Eliminates rework.","sug":"No suggestion","obs":{"MX":"We agree with this for Mexico; we are fine with including it for us.","CO":"This matter has been mentioned in another comment.","CL":"No comments.","USA":"Offender model"}}};
